hadiths[605]{hadithnumber,text}:
"10286","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, who said: He marries her when her waiting period ends."
"10287","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that Sulayman and Ibn al-Musayyab differed: al-Zuhri said: She has her dower, while Sulayman said: Her dower is in the public treasury."
"10288","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Tulayhah bint Ubayd Allah married Rushayd al-Thaqafi during her waiting period. Umar flogged her with the stick and ruled: Any man who marries a woman in her waiting period and touches her, they are separated, then they never join again; she completes the rest of her waiting period from the first, then begins her waiting period from the latter. If he did not touch her, they are separated until she completes the rest of her waiting period from the first, then he proposes to her along with the suitors. Al-Zuhri said: I do not know how much that flogging reached. He said: And Abd al-Malik flogged each of them forty lashes in that; Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb was asked about that and said: Had you lightened and flogged twenty each."
"10289","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Abd Allah ibn Utbah that Umar ibn al-Khattab separated a woman who married in her waiting period from her husband, then ruled: Any woman who marries in her waiting period and her husband has not gone in to her, they are separated; she observes what remains of her waiting period. When it ends, her latter husband proposes along with the suitors; if she wishes she marries him, and if she wishes she leaves him. If he had gone in to her, they are separated, then they never join again; she completes her waiting period from the first, then observes waiting from the latter."
"10290","From Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abd al-Karim and Amr reported to me, one adding over the other, that Rushayd ibn Uthman ibn Amir of Banu Mu'attib al-Thaqafi married Tulayhah bint Ubayd Allah, sister of Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, in the remainder of her waiting period from another; Umar ibn al-Khattab said: If he had gone in to her, they are separated, then he never marries her; she has the dower for what he took of her. Then she observes the rest of her waiting period, then observes waiting from this one; if he had not gone in, she observes the rest of her waiting period, then he marries her if she wishes. I said: They mentioned flogging. He said."
"10291","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, who said: Rushayd al-Thaqafi married a woman in her waiting period; Umar separated them and commanded her to observe the rest of her waiting period from the first, then begin another waiting period from Rushayd."
"10292","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Umar said about the one married in her waiting period: Her dower is in the public treasury, and they do not join."
"10293","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab assigned to the one married in her waiting period her full dower for what he took of her; they are separated and never marry; she observes waiting from both of them."
"10294","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibrahim, about the one married in her waiting period. He said: She completes the rest of her waiting period from the first, then observes a new waiting period from the latter. Al-Sha'bi said: She observes waiting from the latter, then observes the rest of her waiting period from it."
"10295","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, who said: When two waiting periods gather in one waiting period, one waiting period suffices her for both."
"10296","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, concerning a woman divorced by her husband, then a man married her during her waiting period, and she menstruated three menses with him without him touching her, then this came to light. He said: she is separated from him, and these menses are not counted. And another said: they are counted."
"10297","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr. He said: it is counted thereby."
"10298","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a woman who married with five days remaining of her waiting period. He said: they are separated, and her first husband retains the right of return over her during the five days, and she observes it only when she is separated from the other husband. Ma'mar said: al-Zuhri said: he has no right of return over her, even if the five days expired while she was with the other husband, her waiting period has expired. Ayyub said the same from Abu Qilabah."
"10299","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Urwah, from Ali ibn al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, concerning a man who divorces his wife one or two divorces, then another man marries her during her waiting period. He said: they are separated, and her first husband has no right of return over her except by a new proposal, because her waiting period expired with this other man."
"10300","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He was asked about a man who married a woman, then her pregnancy from her first husband became apparent while she was with the other husband. He said: they are separated, she has her dower for what he made lawful of her, and she is returned to her first husband, and if he had divorced her only once or twice, he shall not approach her until she delivers her pregnancy."
"10301","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a woman who married during her waiting period, then her husband consummated with her and she became pregnant by him. He said: they are separated, she waits until she delivers her pregnancy, then she completes her waiting period from the first. Ma'mar said: it reached me something similar from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"10302","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: she completes her waiting period from the latter and from the former."
"10303","From Ma'mar, from Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim. He said: when two waiting periods gather into one waiting period, a single waiting period suffices for both. Al-Thawri said: if she became pregnant by the latter, the child belongs to the former."
"10304","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a woman married during her waiting period. He said: if she had menstruated once before the other married her, then became pregnant, the child belongs to the latter. And it is said: if he impregnated her and they were separated while she is pregnant, she observes what remains of her waiting period from the first at the moment she delivers the pregnancy of the latter. And if she was told her husband died while he was in another land, so she observed the waiting period then married, then this reached her husband and he divorced her, she observes the waiting period from the latter first, then from her first husband, because separation between her and her other husband became due at the moment of his marrying her, before his divorcing her."
"10305","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man who divorced his wife without making it final, then unknowingly married her sister at the end of the divorce waiting period and consummated with her. They both said: they are separated, and she has her dower for what he made lawful of her. They both said: likewise a man who has four wives, divorces one without making it final, then marries another woman during the remainder of the waiting period of the divorced one."
"10306","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man divorced a woman without making it final, then she became pregnant, and he married her sister at the end of her waiting period and consummated with her, then he made both of them final before the waiting period of the divorced one expired. Or a man had four wives, divorced one without making it final, and married another during her waiting period and consummated with her. He said: he is separated from the one he married, then the one he married observes a waiting period from him within the waiting period of the divorced one, so both observe a waiting period from him together. The first observes from him as before, from the day he divorced her, and the latter observes a fresh waiting period from the day they are separated. The first does not wait until she finishes then the latter observes separately, but rather both together. And Abd al-Karim said the same."
"10307","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: and people say: two sisters should not observe waiting periods together, but when the first completes her waiting period, this one observes from him."
"10308","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to him, meaning Ata: a man married a woman during her waiting period from another, and during her waiting period from him, then he divorced her without making it final, then married her sister during her waiting period. He said: we return it and he returns the inheritance, even if fifty years passed. Then he said afterwards: when a long time has passed for that, he does not return it. He said: and Abd al-Karim said: it is returned, even if a long time passed for that, always."
"10309","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata. He said: every marriage not in the manner of marriage, when the two are separated, he shall not marry during that waiting period. And Abd al-Karim said: he shall not marry her."
"10310","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man who has four wives then makes one final. He said: he may marry if he wishes before the waiting period of the fourth expires; he is the furthest of people from her. And Ibn Shihab said: and likewise for two sisters. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, the same."
"10311","From Ibn Jurayj. Ibn Tawus informed us from his father. He said: let him marry as soon as he makes her final, when the man has divorced her in the manner of divorce."
"10312","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: there is no harm in marrying when he divorced her decisively, three times, because he does not inherit her nor does she inherit him. Ma'mar said: al-Hasan said the same."
"10313","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I was informed from Salim ibn Abd Allah, concerning four wives with a man, and he divorced one of them: may he marry before her waiting period ends. He said: a man from Thaqif came and spoke to Uthman ibn Affan about the like of this, and Uthman said to him: when you divorce three times, she neither inherits you nor do you inherit her, so marry if you wish."
"10314","From al-Thawri, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, I do not know it except from Zayd ibn Thabit. He said: when he divorces the fourth of his wives, he shall not marry until the waiting period of the one he divorced expires."
"10315","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah. He said: al-Walid ibn Uqbah had four wives, he divorced one of them three times, then married before her waiting period expired, so Marwan separated between them."
"10316","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb. He said: Marwan, while he was governor, was brought a case of a man who had four wives, divorced one decisively, then married a fifth during her waiting period. Ibn Abbas called out to him while sitting in a side of the house: separate between them during the waiting period of the one he divorced."
"10317","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah. He said: al-Walid ibn Uqbah had four wives, he divorced one decisively, then married a fifth during her waiting period. Ibn Abbas called out to him while sitting in a side of the house: separate between them until the term of the one he divorced expires."
"10318","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. He said: Ali was asked about a man who had a wife, divorced her so she became separated from him, then married her sister during her waiting period. He said: they are separated. From Ibn Jurayj, that the like of that reached him from Ali."
"10319","Ibn Jurayj said: and Abd al-Karim al-Jazari narrated to me: he asked Ibn al-Musayyab about that, and he said: he shall not marry until the waiting period of the first expires."
"10320","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ibn al-Musayyab. He said: concerning the four, when he divorces one of them, he shall not marry until the waiting period of the fourth expires."
"10321","From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that he disliked it. He said: and they say the like of that concerning two sisters."
"10322","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin. He said: it was reported from Abidah that he said: there is no harm in that. He said: I said: do you not dislike that a man be with two sisters from me. He said: yes, so he shall not marry her. So he retracted his statement."
"10323","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid. He said: when a man has four wives and divorces one, he shall not marry until the waiting period of the one he divorced expires."
"10324","From Ibn Abi Yahya, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Isa, from al-Sha'bi. He said: when he divorces the fourth, he shall not marry the fifth until the waiting period of the one he divorced expires. Ibn Abi Yahya said: and it was confirmed for us from Ali and Ibn Abbas the same."
"10325","From al-Thawri, from Abu Hashim al-Wasiti. He said: I said to al-Nakha'i: is there a waiting period upon the man. He said: yes, and two waiting periods. He said: I said: and two. He said: yes, and three. He said: then he mentioned two sisters, divorcing one of them, and four wives, divorcing one of them, and a man under whom is a woman who has a son from other than her husband, then her son dies, so her husband should not approach her until it is clear whether she is pregnant or not, so that he inherits his brother or does not inherit him."
"10326","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Layth, from al-Hakam, that al-Hasan ibn Ali said to a man from Banu Hashim who married a woman having a son from other than him, then that son of hers died, so he commanded him not to approach her until she menstruates or until it is known there is no pregnancy in her."
"10327","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a woman whose son dies while she has a husband. He said: he shall not touch her until it is known whether she is pregnant or not. When that is known, he may have her if he wishes. And Ma'mar used to say it. Ma'mar said: so that he inherits his brother or does not inherit him."
"10328","Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Bishr al-A'rabi informed us. He said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us. He said: we read from al-Thawri, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani, that a Bedouin man married off a daughter of his, drove her dower and took possession of it. When the father died, she came disputing for her dower, and her brothers came. The brothers said: our father took possession of it in his lifetime. The woman said: it is my dower. Umar said: what you find in kind, you have more right to it, and what your father consumed, you have no debt upon your father for it."
"10329","From al-Thawri, from al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, that Shurayh imprisoned a man for his daughter's dower of six hundred."
"10330","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I asked Ata about a man who proposed on behalf of his absent son, and said: if my son refuses, then I will. He said: this cannot be in marriage. And Abd al-Karim said the same."
"10331","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning a man who proposed on behalf of a man, so they married him off, then the one proposed for came and denied. He said: I did not command him with anything. They both said: upon the proposer is half the dower. Al-Zuhri said: if evidence stands for the messenger that he sent him, the right is established upon the husband, otherwise he swears. Al-Zuhri said: and there is no waiting period upon her."
"10332","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Shubrumah. He said: there is no marriage between them."
"10333","From al-Thawri. He said: there is nothing upon the proposer messenger, unless there is evidence against the sender, or the messenger is a guarantor. If the sender dies before denying, upon her is the waiting period, and she has nothing."
"10334","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Shubrumah: concerning a man who married a woman, he in one land and she in another, then he died. If evidence stands that he had taken possession of her and she consented before he died, she has inheritance and dower."
"10335","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: it is established by the marriage, until they bring evidence that he died before the marriage; the evidence is upon his heirs."
"10336","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata. He said: I said: a man married off his absent father, and the father did not approve. Upon whom is the dower. He said: upon the father."
"10337","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who married a woman conditioned upon divorcing another. He said: some people say: if he marries her conditioned upon divorcing her fellow wife, that is a dower for her. We do not say that. She has the dower of her likes, and no divorce falls upon the other until he divorces."
"10338","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who married a woman on condition of lending her a thousand dirhams, and he brought her a thousand dirhams. He said: this is nothing. She has the dower of her likes among her women."
"10339","From al-Thawri, concerning a man who married a woman for a writ of debt upon a man. He said: she has the dower of her likes, and the marriage is valid."
"10340","From al-Thawri. He said: if a man married a woman and gave her a slave, then he turns out stolen. He said: as for Shurayh, he said: the value. Ibn Abi Layla said it. As for us, we say: she has the dower of her likes if he was free."
"10341","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Qays, from a grandmother of his. She said: I disputed with my father before Shurayh concerning a maidservant of mine whom a wife of his gave as dower. He ruled the maidservant for me, and ruled upon my father to pay his wife its value."
"10342","From Ibn al-Taymi, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid. He said: Amir was asked about a man who married a woman on condition of freeing her father, but he was not sold. He said: his value is assessed, then its price is paid to her."
"10343","From Ma'mar. He said: I asked Ibn Shubrumah about a man who married a woman for an unspecified youth servant. He said: an Arab, an Indian, and an Abyssinian are assessed, and a third of their values is taken."
"10344","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I asked Ata about a man who married a woman and stipulated upon him: if you bring the dower by such time, she is your wife, otherwise not. The term came and he did not bring it. He said: once they married him off, he has more right to her. Ibn Jurayj said: Abd al-Karim said the same."
"10345","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Ibn Abbas, concerning a man who married a woman, and they stipulated upon him: if the dower comes by a named term, she is his wife, and if he does not bring it by that term, she is not his wife. He said: judgment was given for the man for his wife, and he said: there is nothing in their stipulation."
"10346","From Ma'mar, from a man, from al-Hasan. He said: in this, the marriage is valid and the condition is void."
"10347","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: if he does not bring the dower by the term, there is no marriage between them."
"10348","From Ma'mar, from Mansur, from Ibrahim. He said: every condition in marriage is void, when it is stipulated: you shall not marry nor take a concubine, and the like, except if he says: if I do such and such, she is divorced, then that binds him."
"10349","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man married a woman, and it was stipulated upon him: you shall not marry nor take a concubine nor take her out. He said: the condition does not go away once he married her."
"10350","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim. He said: every condition in marriage, the marriage demolishes it, except divorce. And every condition in a sale, the sale demolishes it, except manumission."
"10351","From al-Thawri, from Tariq, from al-Sha'bi: concerning a man who stipulates for the woman at her marriage that she keeps her house. He used to consider it nothing. He said: her husband is her house."
"10352","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: their stipulation is nothing. Ma'mar said: al-Hasan said that. He said: he may take her out if he wishes. Ma'mar said: Qatadah said the same."
"10353","From al-Thawri, from al-Ash'ath, from Adi ibn Artah. He said: I came to Shurayh and said: a man from the people of Sham. He said: welcome. He said: I said: where are you. He said: below the wall. He said: I said: may I come near you. He said: your tongue is longer than your hand. He said: I married a woman. He said: with harmony and sons. I said: her house was stipulated for her. He said: the condition has more authority. He said: I said: may I take her out. He said: you have more right to her. He said: I said: judge between us. He said: I have finished."
"10354","From Hisham, from Muhammad, from Shurayh, that he permitted the condition and ruled for her by it."
"10355","From more than one, that a man and his wife came to Shurayh. The man said: where are you. He said: below the wall. He said: I am a man from the people of Sham. He said: far, hateful. He said: I married this woman. He said: with harmony and sons. He said: she bore me a boy. He said: may the horseman congratulate you. He said: I wanted to go out with her to Sham. He said: accompanied. He said: and she stipulated her house for herself. He said: the condition has more authority. He said: judge between us, may Allah keep you right. He said: narrate two narrations to a woman, if she refuses then four. Abd al-Razzaq said: other than Ma'mar says: narrate two narrations to a man, if he refuses then four."
"10356","From Ayyub, from Isma'il ibn Ubayd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. He said: I witnessed Umar ibn al-Khattab, and a dispute was brought to him concerning a woman whose husband stipulated for her not to take her out of her house. Umar said: she has her condition. A man said: if it is so, no woman wishing to part from her husband but will part from him. Umar said: Muslims are bound by their stipulations, at the limits of their shares."
"10357","Ma'mar informed us. He said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, that a man married a woman and stipulated not to marry over her, nor take a concubine, nor move her to his family. This reached Umar, and he said: I adjure you but to marry over her, take a concubine, and take her out to your family."
"10358","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: al-Ajlah informed me, from Adi ibn Adi, from Isma'il ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm. He said: I was sitting beside Umar ibn al-Khattab, his thigh upon my thigh or my thigh upon his, when a woman came disputing her husband. She said: I stipulated for myself when he married me that he would not take me out of Madinah. Umar said: she has her stipulation."
"10359","From al-Thawri, from al-Ajlah, from Adi ibn Adi, from a man, from Umar. He said: a woman was brought to him whom a man married and stipulated her house for her. Umar said: fulfill her condition for her."
"10360","From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri, that Abd al-Karim informed them, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud. He said: Mu'awiyah was brought a case of a woman whose husband stipulated for her that she keeps her house. He asked Amr ibn al-As, and he said: I see he should fulfill her condition."
"10361","From Ibn al-Mubarak, from Layth ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu al-Khayr, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The most deserving of conditions you fulfill are those by which you made private parts lawful. From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I was narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the same."
"10362","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abu al-Sha'tha, that he said: when her family stipulates upon her husband: her house is our house, and you shall not take her out, it is a dower for her, and she may refuse him taking her out. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, the same."
"10363","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he asked Tawus. He said: I said: a woman stipulates at marriage: I stay with my family, do not take me out from them. He said: every Muslim woman who stipulated a condition upon a man by which he made her private part lawful, it is not lawful for him but to fulfill. Abu al-Zubayr said: and I heard Abu al-Sha'tha saying: every woman who stipulated upon her husband, by which he made her private part lawful, it is part of her dower. And they said: if they stipulate: you divorce so-and-so, do not do it, because the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade a woman asking for the divorce of another."
"10364","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man married a woman, and she stipulated upon him: if you marry or take a concubine or take me out, I have such and such wealth upon you. He said: if he marries, she has that wealth upon him. He said: it is part of her dower."
"10365","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: it is an addition in her dower."
"10366","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: they stipulated upon him: if you mistreat, her authority is in our hands, and she is divorced. Then they established mistreatment of her. He said: they have not what they stipulated until he divorces, but holding with kindness or releasing with goodness."
"10367","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Ata, concerning a man marrying a woman, and it is stipulated upon him at the marriage contract: if you take her out, she is divorced. He said: if he takes her out, she is divorced."
"10368","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah: if he did not utter it after the marriage contract, it is nothing."
"10369","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Sha'bi, concerning a man who married a woman for a thousand, and if you have a wife then two thousand. He said: the marriage is valid, and she has the lesser of the two."
"10370","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abbad ibn Abi Layla, from al-Minhal, from Abd Allah, from Ali. He said: a man was brought to him who married a woman and stipulated her house for her. He said: Allah's condition is before their condition. He did not consider it anything."
"10371","From Muhammad ibn Rashid. He said: Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah informed me. He said: I asked four: al-Hasan, Abd al-Rahman ibn Udhaynah, Iyas ibn Mu'awiyah, and Hisham ibn Hubayrah, about a man who married a woman and stipulated her house for her. They said: her stipulation is nothing; he may take her out if he wishes."
"10372","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: Abd al-Karim informed me that Abu Musa informed him that two guardians, both valid in marriage, one married Ubayd Allah ibn al-Hurr al-Ju'fi, and the other married another. Ubayd Allah was married before the gathering of the other. Ali ibn Abi Talib ruled her for Ubayd Allah. He said: and Abu Musa is a neighbor of Ubayd Allah. He said: it reached me from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah: Ali ruled for Ubayd Allah, and she has her dower upon the other for what he took of her, and that she is Ju'fiyyah."
"10373","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah. He said: she is the wife of the first. If the other had entered with her, they are separated, she has the dower, and the other shall not approach her until her waiting period expires."
"10374","From Abd Allah ibn Muharrar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any woman married off by two guardians of hers, she belongs to the first of them. And whoever sells a sale to two men, the sale belongs to the first. From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Uqbah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"10375","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I was informed from al-Hasan, that he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When two guardians marry off, the first counts."
"10376","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh. He said: when two authorizing guardians marry off, the marriage belongs to the first."
"10377","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata. He said: the marriage belongs to the first, unless the other entered. If he entered with her, he has more right to her. Ibn Jurayj said: and Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that Mu'awiyah ruled like the statement of Ata."
"10378","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: if two guardians marry off, this one in one land and this one in another, the marriage belongs to the first, unless the other entered with her, and the other did not know of her marriage. If he entered with her, she is his wife."
"10379","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan. He said: I think it is from Uqbah ibn Amir, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Any woman married off by two guardians of hers, the marriage belongs to the first. Qatadah said: if the other entered with her, they are separated, she has the dower, the first shall not approach her until her waiting period expires, and she has the dower upon him."
"10380","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that Musa ibn Talhah married Yazid ibn Mu'awiyah in Sham to Umm Ishaq daughter of Talhah, and Ya'qub ibn Talhah married her to al-Hasan ibn Ali. Musa married before Ya'qub. She stayed only two or three nights until al-Hasan ibn Ali consummated with her. When this reached Mu'awiyah, he said: a woman her husband has consummated with, leave her. He said: and Musa is the guardian of her property, and both are her brothers by her father."
"10381","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a Christian man who married his Muslim daughter to a Muslim man, and a brother of hers married her to a Muslim man. He said: the marriage of her brother is valid."
"10382","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata. He said: if two men marry off a woman and it is not known which married first, her marriage is rejected, then she marries whichever she wishes."
"10383","From Ma'mar: and he was asked about two guardians, each married a man, and it is not known which married first. He said: I heard nothing in this, except that Qatadah said: concerning two slaves, each bought his fellow from his master, and it is not known which bought his fellow first. He said: when it is not known, there is no sale between them. If it is known which bought first, the sale is valid, as if he analogized it with them. Ma'mar said: and I heard one saying: each is compelled to a divorce until she becomes lawful to one who marries her."
"10384","From al-Thawri. He said: when the woman says to two guardians: marry me off, and one married her off without the command of the other, it is nothing until both approve her. And when she says to this one: marry me off, and to this one: marry me off, and it is known which is first, his marriage is valid. If it is not known, each husband is given choice to a divorce. If they refuse, the ruler separates a separation, and she has no dower. Then whichever she wishes marries her. And he said concerning two slaves, one buying his fellow, not known which is first. He said: rejected."
"10385","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man marries a woman, how long stays with the virgin without apportioning for the other. He said: what do you think, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: three days for the virgin, and two days for the previously married."
"10386","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas. He said: seven for the virgin, and three for the previously married."
"10387","From al-Thawri, from Ayyub and Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas. He said: the practice is to stay with the virgin seven, and with the previously married three. If you wish I would say: he raised it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"10388","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: Habib ibn Abi Thabit informed me, that Abd al-Hamid ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Amr and al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed him that they heard Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informing that Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him: when she arrived Madinah, she told them she is the daughter of Abu Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah. He said: they disbelieved her, saying: how lying are strangers, until some of them set out to Hajj. They said: will you write to your family. She wrote with them. They returned to Madinah believing her, and she increased in honor with them. She said: when I delivered Zaynab, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and proposed to me. I said: one like me is not married; I am old, jealous, with dependents. He said: I am older than you, as for jealousy Allah will remove it, as for dependents then to Allah and His Messenger. He married her. He would come to her saying: where is Zunab, until Ammar ibn Yasir came and took her away. He said: this one prevents the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and she was nursing her. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came and said: where is Zunab. She said: the daughter of Qaribah daughter of Abu Umayyah, and she agreed with her at her place, Ammar ibn Yasir took her. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I am coming to you tonight. She said: I stood, put my grinding stones, took out grains of barley from my jar, took out fat and made porridge for him. She said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spent the night, then morning came. When morning came he said: you have honor with your family; if you wish I stay seven with you, and if I stay seven I stay seven for my wives."
"10389","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father. He said: when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married Umm Salamah and consummated with her, he said: you have no humiliation with your family; if I stay seven I stay seven for my wives, otherwise three then I rotate."
"10390","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bakr ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from his father. He said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stayed with Umm Salamah three days when he consummated with her, then said: you have no humiliation with your family; if I stay seven for you I stay seven for my wives."
"10391","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from al-Hasan. He said: three for the virgin, and two nights for the previously married. From Yunus, from al-Hasan, the same."
"10392","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan and Ibn al-Musayyab. They both said: he stays with the virgin three days, then stays with the previously married two days, then apportions."
"10393","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: three for the virgin. He said: and Ibn Ishaq said it from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, also."
"10394","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man proposes to a woman, having a wife, and proposes to her that you have a day, and so-and-so two days, at proposal before marriage. He said: that is valid before marriage, and after they agreed upon that. I said: concerning that was revealed: If a woman fears cruelty or desertion from her husband. He said: yes. I said: did the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do that with some of his wives. He said: yes. He said: I said: what is: And souls are swayed by greed. He said: concerning maintenance; they claim that woman was Sawdah."
"10395","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah. He said: there is no harm in that."
"10396","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: Ibn al-Musayyab and Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me that Rafi' ibn Khadij had under him a woman advanced in age, then married a young woman over her, preferring the young over her. His first wife refused to remain upon that, so he divorced her once until when little remained of her term. He said: if you wish I return to you and you endure preference, and if you wish I leave you until your term ends. She said: rather return to me and I endure preference. He returned to her, preferring the other, but she did not endure preference, so he divorced her another, preferring the young. He said: that is the settlement we were told Allah revealed concerning it: If a woman fears cruelty or desertion from her husband. From Ma'mar. He said: Ayyub informed me, from Ibn Sirin, from Abidah, like the narration of al-Zuhri, adding: if he harms her in the third, she may have him fulfill her right or divorce her."
"10397","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that Sawdah gave her day to A'ishah."
"10398","From al-Thawri, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit. He said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intended to part with Sawdah, so he called Abu Bakr and Umar to witness her divorce. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no desire in the world except to be gathered on Resurrection Day among your wives, so I have of reward what they have."
"10399","From Abu Hanifah, from al-Haytham or Abu al-Haytham, Abu Bakr doubted, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divorced Sawdah once. She sat for him in his path; when he passed she asked him return, and to give her share from him to whichever of his wives he wishes, hoping to be raised on Resurrection Day as his wife. He returned to her and accepted that."
"10400","From Ma'mar. He said: it reached me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, intended to part with Sawdah, so she spoke to him concerning that. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I have no eagerness of wives, but I love Allah to raise me on Resurrection Day as a wife for you."
"10401","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: it is disliked a man proposes to a woman stipulating you have a day and so-and-so two days. He says: settlement is only after entry, not before entry."
"10402","From Ma'mar: concerning a man who married a woman and stipulated upon her he prefers another wife of his over her, then he changed his mind afterwards. He said: she has that; their stipulation is nothing. And he mentioned like the narration of Abidah: If a woman fears cruelty or desertion from her husband."
"10403","From al-Thawri, concerning a man marrying a woman on condition you have a day and so-and-so two days. He said: the condition is void; she has the practice. From more than one."
"10404","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, concerning a man marrying while sick. He said: I see it only as an innovation; his marriage is not valid. If he recovers in between, it is valid."
"10405","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, concerning a man who married while sick. He said: he may not bring harm upon the people of inheritance, and we do not see she inherits him if he did that to harm."
"10406","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah. He said: if he married her from need of her in service or care, she inherits him. Ma'mar said: and Rabi'ah ibn Abi Layla said: her dower and inheritance are in the third."
"10407","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim. He said: he marries in his illness, and it is not counted from the third."
"10408","From al-Thawri, concerning a man marrying while sick. He said: his marriage is valid upon the dower of her likes."
"10409","From Abu Hanifah: concerning a man sick, who freed a slavegirl of his, then married her and gave her dower, then died. He said: her freeing is valid in the third, and her dower from the principal wealth."
"10410","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man marries sick then dies in his illness. He said: I see it only as an innovation. Ata said: if he recovers in between, what she took is valid. If he was sick, visited from it, then died, his marriage is not valid."
"10411","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Nafi', that Abd Allah ibn Abi Rabi'ah married the daughter of Hafs ibn al-Mughirah while sick, to share his wives in inheritance, and there was kinship between them."
"10412","From al-Thawri, and I asked him, about a man sick, who said to a woman: marry this son of mine, your dower of a thousand dirhams is upon me, while the dower of her likes is five hundred dirhams, then he died of that illness. He said: it is valid for her upon him, and the heirs take from his son, for he is but a guarantor. I said: if his son did not command him to marry him off. He said: even so upon him, whether he commanded or not."
"10413","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: I said to Ata: a man marries in his illness. He said: if it was an illness visited from it, then he dies of it, it is not valid. If he sickens then recovers in between, what she took is valid."
"10414","Ibn Jurayj informed us. He said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Ikrimah ibn Khalid saying: Ibn Umm al-Hakam in his illness wanted to exclude his wife from her inheritance, but she refused. He married over her three women, dowering them a thousand dinars each, and Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan permitted it, sharing them in the eighth."
"10415","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata. He said: it reached us that a leprous, insane, vitiliginous, or slit woman is not valid in marriage nor sale. He said: I said: if he consummated with her having one of the four, and the guardian knew then concealed it. He said: I see only he owes her dower for what he took of her except a small part of it. He said: I said: if other than a guardian married her off. He said: it is returned to the dower of her likes."
"10416","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I heard Amr ibn Dinar saying: Abu al-Sha'tha said: four are not valid in marriage nor sale unless named; if named, she is of him: the insane, leprous, vitiliginous, and slit. If he touched her it is valid, even if deceived. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Sha'tha the same. From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Sha'tha the same."
"10417","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali. He said: return is for vaginal closure, leprosy, insanity, and vitiligo. If he entered with her, upon him is the dower; if he wishes he divorces her, if he wishes he does not divorce, if he wishes he keeps. If he did not enter with her, they are separated. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Isma'il, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi the same."
"10418","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyab. He said: I heard him saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: any woman married having insanity, leprosy, or vitiligo. Ibn Jurayj said: I do not know with which he began. Then he entered with her, then discovered that, she has her dower. Ibn Jurayj said: for his touching her. And upon the guardian is the dower for concealing by deceiving him."
"10419","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab. He said: I heard him saying: when a man deceives a man with a woman and he enters with her, she has upon him her dower for what he made lawful of her, and her husband takes from the wealth of the one who deceived for him. If he knew before entering with her, his marriage is valid."
"10420","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: if the guardian knew, he is fined, otherwise he is made to swear by Allah he did not know, then it is upon the husband. Ma'mar said: Qatadah said it. Ma'mar said: it reached me if he did not consummate with her he has choice; if he wishes he parts her, if he wishes he keeps her. Ma'mar said: if something resembles these ailments, it is like it."
"10421","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: the imperforate woman is returned in marriage. The imperforate is she whom a man cannot approach."
"10422","From Abd al-Rahman, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, that Adi ibn Adi, governor of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, informed him. He said: a man and woman he married came to us; when he entered with her he found her imperforate, fused bones, no man can overpower her, having only a passage of water. I wrote concerning her to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. He wrote to me: make the guardian swear he did not know; if he swears, permit the marriage, for I think no man pleased with marrying among a people but will be pleased with their trust. If he does not swear, charge the dower upon him."
"10423","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Maymun ibn Mihran. He said: a woman with something wrong was brought to Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Umar said: I see for him only the trust of his in-laws."
"10424","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub. He said: it was reported from Ibn Sirin. He said: a man disputed to Shurayh. He said: these said to me: we marry you to the most beautiful of people, then they brought me a bleary-eyed woman. He said: if he concealed a defect from you, it is not valid."
"10425","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: Ibn Tawus informed me from his father. He said: deception is not valid."
"10426","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim. He said: a free woman is not returned for a defect as a slavegirl is returned; he is a man afflicted."
"10427","From Ma'mar. He said: it reached me that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz and al-Hasan said: there is no liability in women; when her husband consummates with her, her dower is due upon him. He said: and I thought it reached me from Ali like their statement."
"10428","From al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, that a man proposed his daughter to him, and she had done something new to him. He came to Umar and mentioned that to him. Umar said: what did you see of her. He said: I saw only good. He said: marry her off and do not inform."
"10429","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi. He said: a man came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I buried a daughter of mine alive in ignorance, reaching her before she died and taking her out. Then she reached Islam with us and her Islam was good. She committed a hadd offense of Islam, and we were surprised only she took a knife to slaughter herself. I rescued her, her soul had come out, I treated her until her wound healed, and she turned with good turning. She was proposed to me, shall I mention what was of her. Umar said: Hah, if you do I will punish you a punishment. Abu Farwah said: the people of tents and cities hear it. Isma'il said: the people of cities narrate it: marry her off as the marriage of a chaste Muslim woman."
"10430","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: she had committed adultery or theft, and he did not know until he married her, then he was informed before consummating. He said: she has nothing."
"10431","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: she is his wife in every case; he does not part her nor does she part him."
"10432","From al-Thawri, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Sha'bi, concerning she who fornicated before her husband entered with her. He said: the marriage is as it is. Ibrahim said: the dower is returned, and they are separated."
"10433","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah. He said: when she innovates before he enters with her, he parts her, and she has nothing."
"10434","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Ala ibn Jabir. He said: a woman fornicated in the time of Ali, married but not entered with. He said: she was brought to Ali, he lashed her a hundred, exiled her a year to Nahr Karbala, then she returned and he returned her to her husband by her first marriage."
"10435","From Isra'il ibn Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash. He said: Ali was brought a man who committed adultery with a woman, married a woman but did not enter with her. He said: did you commit adultery. He said: yes, and I was not married. He said: he commanded him, he was lashed a hundred, separated between him and his wife, and gave her half the dower."
"10436","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, concerning a man lashed for adultery hadd then married a woman without informing her. He said: if he entered with her, she has her dower, and she parts him if she wishes. If he did not enter with her, she has half the dower, and she parts him if she wishes. He said: if she was the punished one, and he entered with her unknowing, she has her dower, and the one who deceived her for him is fined. If the guardian did not know of her, nothing is upon him. If he did not enter with her, he is given choice, and she has no dower."
"10437","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri. He said: the marriage is established as it is."
"10438","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Tawus, from his father. They both said: when a man is lashed a hadd for adultery, then marries, if repentance is seen of him, they remain upon their marriage. Ma'mar said: and I heard one saying: returned of marriage is what is returned of necks."
"10439","From al-Thawri, concerning a man afflicted with a calamity, they are not separated. He is in the position of the woman; the man is not returned nor the woman. He mentioned it from Hammad, from Ibrahim."
"10440","From Ibn Jurayj. He said: I said to Ata: a man having one of the four: leprosy, insanity, vitiligo, or slit. He said: she has nothing; he has more right to her."
"10441","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man afflicted with vitiligo, or leprosy, or insanity, or something like that, who married a woman while she did not know of his condition until he consummated the marriage with her: he said, she has the choice, and she gets her dower; but if she knew before consummation, she gets half the dower. Ma'mar said: al-Zuhri said, she gets nothing, and this is the dearer of the two opinions to Ma'mar."
"10442","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrating that a woman during the governorship of Ibn Alqamah was married by a man, and after time passed with him, he was informed that she had committed adultery before he married her; so he wrote to Abd al-Malik about her: what do you think is due for her? So he wrote: upon her is the curse of Allah; take back his wealth for him, and carry out the limits of Allah upon her."
"10443","Ibrahim ibn Muhammad reported to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from a man of the Ansar called Busrah, he said: I married a virgin woman and came to her, and she turned out to be pregnant; so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: she gets the dower for what was made lawful of her private part, and the child is a slave for you, and when she gives birth, then flog her. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: it was narrated to me from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, the like of it."
"10444","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: what do you think, if he had intercourse with her while she had one of the four defects and he did not know — what of her guardian who knew and then concealed it from her? He said: I see only that he has become liable for her dower except something of it for what he took of her; and this is only an opinion I hold. He said: and she gets her dower in full. I said: then one other than her guardian married her off? He said: she is returned to her dower for what he took of her."
"10445","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: is the man in the position of the woman in that, if he has one of the four defects? He said: she gets nothing; he has more right to her."
"10446","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib said: whatever affliction a man has of a condition whose harm is not confined to him alone, she has the choice regarding him when she learns of it; if she wishes she stays with him, and if she wishes she leaves him; and whatever of it is confined to him alone, his marriage is valid."
"10447","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that a woman of Sanaa was married by a man, and he had not yet joined her when he became leprous; so she sent to him: separate from her, and your dower is yours; but he refused; so Muhammad ibn Yusuf wrote about that to Abd al-Malik, and Abd al-Malik wrote: separate between them. The name of the man was Awsajah ibn Anas ibn Dawud, of the Abna, and the name of the woman was Umm Amr bint Barasa ibn Sa'd."
"10448","From Ma'mar, he said: Ibn Abi Najih narrated to us that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan judged concerning a woman whom a man married, then he became leprous before consummation with her: he separated between them and returned the dower to him. Ibn Abi Najih said, from Mujahid: I do not think they should be separated, and he is in greatest need of her at that time."
"10449","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, they said: if that befell him after he had married her, then they remain upon their marriage, even if he had not yet entered with her."
"10450","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that he judged concerning a man who sought a woman in marriage from her father, and she had an Arab mother, and he gave him in marriage; but she had a sister from her father by a non-Arab mother, and the daughter of the non-Arab woman was brought in to him and he had intercourse with her; then in the morning he found her objectionable; so he judged: the dower belongs to the one he entered with, and he assigned to him the daughter of the Arab woman, and he placed her dower upon her father, and he said: he shall not enter with her until the waiting period of her sister has passed. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad ibn Murrah narrated to me that Ali judged likewise in a similar case."
"10451","From Ma'mar, from Budayl al-Uqayli, from Abu al-Wadi', and he was a companion of Ali, he said: Ali judged concerning a man who married off a daughter of his, but he sent her sister and presented her to her husband: Ali judged for the one he consummated with what is in her house, and upon her father to prepare the other at his own expense and then send her to her husband."
"10452","From Isra'il, from Simak, from Salih ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, that a man had five daughters and he married off one of them to a man, but her sister was conducted to him as a bride; so Ali said: she gets the dower for what was made lawful of her private part, and upon her father is the dower of this one for her husband, and upon him to conduct her to him as a bride; and if he came to her deliberately, then the hadd is upon him."
"10453","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: he used to say in cases like this: the father is flogged one hundred as exemplary punishment."
"10454","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: the one he consummated with gets her dower from her husband, and it is due from her father to her husband; and the first one is his wife, and he shall not approach her until the waiting period of the one he had intercourse with ends, if he did not know."
"10455","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, he said: Ibn Shihab was asked about a eunuch who married a free woman; he said: there is no harm in a eunuch marrying if she is pleased."
"10456","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, he said: Ali said: it is not lawful for a eunuch to marry a chaste Muslim woman."
"10457","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyib, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab judged concerning one who is unable to approach women that he be given a delay of a year. Ma'mar said: and it reached me that he is given a delay of a year from the day she raises her case."
"10458","From Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyib, that Umar set for the impotent husband a term of a year, and gave her her dower in full."
"10459","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, that Umar and Ibn Mas'ud judged that she waits with him a year, then after the year she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman, and he has more right to her during her waiting period."
"10460","From al-Thawri, from al-Rukayn, from his father, and Husayn ibn Qabisah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: the impotent husband is given a delay of a year; then if he enters with her, otherwise they are separated."
"10461","From al-Thawri, from Ibn al-Nu'man, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, he said: an impotent man was brought before him, and he gave him a delay of a year."
"10462","From al-Hasan ibn Umarah, from al-Hakam, from Ali, he said: the impotent husband is given a delay of a year; then if he has intercourse with her, otherwise she has more right to herself."
"10463","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I asked Ata about one who does not approach women; he said: she gets the dower when he closed the door upon her, and she waits with him a year from the day she disputes with him; as for before that, it is pardon she granted him. And Umar said that: then when a year has passed, she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman after the year, and it counts as a divorce; then if he did not divorce her, he has more right to her during the waiting period."
"10464","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: the impotent husband is given a delay of a year; then if he enters with her, otherwise they are separated, and she gets the full dower."
"10465","From Ma'mar, and he was asked about a previously married woman whom a man married, and she claimed that he does not approach her, while he said: yes I do; he said: Qatadah used to narrate from some of the people of knowledge: women should be called to be present until her husband has intercourse with her near them, for that will not be hidden from them."
"10466","I heard Ibn Jurayj saying: that is known when he has intercourse with her — let him show it to them in a cloth. Abd al-Razzaq said: meaning the semen."
"10467","From al-Thawri, about the impotent husband, he said: if the woman was previously married, then the word is his, and he is made to swear; and if she was a virgin, women look at her. Abd al-Razzaq: and this is the best of the sayings on it, and we adopt it."
"10468","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: what do you think, if a woman went ahead with a man while knowing that he does not approach women? He said: she has no claim of speech against him, nor dispute; he has more right to her."
"10469","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: a man who suffers whisperings, though he used to have intercourse with his wife? He said: she has no right, and no claim."
"10470","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar said to me: we heard that if he approached her even once, then she has no claim. He said: I said: is it established? He said: we have continued to hear it."
"10471","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: a man married a woman and stays with her a while having intercourse with her, then he grows old until he no longer approaches women, then she disputes with him? He said: she has no claim, nor right, nor favor, and he has more right to her."
"10472","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Hani ibn Hani al-Hamdani, he said: a woman came to Ali ibn Abi Talib and said: O Commander of the Believers, do you want a woman who is neither widowed nor having a husband? He said: Ali understood what she meant, and said: who is her companion? They said: so-and-so, and he is the chief of his people. He said: then there came an old man bent over, dragging himself along, and he said: are you the companion of this woman? He said: yes, and you see our condition. He said: is there anything besides that? He said: no. He said: not even by magic? He said: no. He said: she is ruined and you have ruined her. She said: what do you command me, may Allah keep you right? He said: fear of Allah and patience; I will not separate between you two. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from Hani ibn Hani, then he mentioned the like of the hadith of al-Thawri."
"10473","From a man, from Aslam, he said: a woman came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and said: her husband does not approach her; so he sent for her husband and asked him, and he said: I have grown old and my strength is gone; so he said to him: in how many days do you approach her? He said: once in every period of purity. So Umar said: go, for in him is what suffices a woman."
"10474","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, he said: Ikrimah was asked about a guardian who married off a woman and stipulated for himself against the husband such-and-such; so Ikrimah said: it belongs to whoever it is done for. Abd al-Razzaq said: and sometimes Ma'mar would say it like this, and sometimes he said: whoever it is done for."
"10475","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whatever woman marries upon a dower, or a gift, or a promised grant before the bond of marriage, then it belongs to her; and whatever is after the bond of marriage, then it belongs to whoever it was given to; and the worthiest for whom a man is honored is his daughter and his sister. He said: I heard al-Muthanna narrating that he heard Amr ibn Shu'ayb narrating that he heard this hadith. Amr said: and Urwah informed me, from Aishah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it. From Ibn Jurayj, from Abdullah ibn Ziyad, that Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi, then he mentioned the like of it."
"10476","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: whatever is stipulated in the marriage of a woman is part of her dower; and Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz judged so concerning a woman of Banu Jumah."
"10477","From al-Thawri, from Thawr, from Makhul, he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whatever you made lawful thereby of the sanctity of the woman, of dower or gift, then it belongs to her; and the worthiest whom a man honors with it is his daughter and his sister."
"10478","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Shubrumah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab judged concerning a guardian who married off a woman and stipulated against her husband something for himself: Umar judged that it is part of her dower."
"10479","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, or another, that Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz said: whatever woman marries upon a dower, or a gift, or a promised grant, when the bond of marriage was upon that, then it belongs to her as part of her dower. He said: and whatever after that of gifts belongs to whoever it was given to; then if he divorces her, she gets half of what the bond of marriage made binding upon him of dower or gift."
"10480","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: whatever woman marries and it is stipulated against her husband that her brother gets such-and-such of the honor-gift, and her mother and her father likewise; he said: that is only part of her dower; then if she speaks concerning it, she has more right to it; and if he divorces her, she gets half of all that; and if he favors them with something besides her dower, then it is not theirs."
"10481","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me that his father used to say: whatever honor-gift they stipulated for themselves in the dower belongs to her dower, and she has more right to it if she speaks."
"10482","From al-Thawri, about the unveiling gift, he said: it is nothing until it is taken possession of."
"10483","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, from Ibn Shihab, that he was asked about the unveiling gift when the man dies; so he said: if he had granted it to her and made witnesses for her, then that is allowed for her from his wealth; and if it was only heard of as a matter, then she gets nothing. And Abd al-Malik judged by it, while Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz did not consider it anything."
"10484","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim informed me that Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed him, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, leaned upon the Ka'bah and admonished the people and reminded them, then said: none shall pray after Asr until night, nor after Fajr until the sun rises, and no woman shall travel except with a mahram for three days, and no woman shall be brought in marriage over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt. From al-Muthanna, he said: Amr ibn Shu'ayb informed me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, then he mentioned the like of it."
"10485","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: it reached us that it is forbidden to join together a woman and her maternal aunt and her paternal aunt through fosterage. He said: they are joined together? He said: no, that is like birth."
"10486","From Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt."
"10487","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that he heard Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman saying: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade joining together a woman and her maternal aunt, or a woman and her paternal aunt. Amr said: as for the daughter of the paternal uncle, I have not heard of it."
"10488","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"10489","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Tawus saying: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade joining together a woman and her paternal aunt, and a woman and her maternal aunt."
"10490","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he used to forbid joining together a woman and her paternal aunt. I said: ever? He said: or the paternal aunt of her father, or the maternal aunt of her father."
"10491","From Ma'mar, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: a woman shall not be married over the daughter of her sister, nor shall a woman be married over her paternal aunt, nor shall a woman be married over her maternal aunt, nor shall a woman be married over the daughter of her brother."
"10492","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"10493","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that he disliked the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt through fosterage."
"10494","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I said to him: does a man join together a woman and her paternal aunt through fosterage? He said: no, that is like birth."
"10495","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, that Ibn Mas'ud said: and I dislike your paternal aunt through fosterage and your maternal aunt."
"10496","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: is she joined with the daughter of her paternal aunt? He said: there is no harm in that."
"10497","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, that he disliked joining together two daughters of paternal uncles."
"10498","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about two daughters of paternal uncles being joined together, he said: it is not unlawful if one does it, but it is because of severing ties."
"10499","From Ma'mar, from a man, from Ikrimah, he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt, for if they do that they sever their kinship ties."
"10500","From al-Thawri, from Khalid ibn Salamah al-Fa'fa', from Ishaq ibn Talhah, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over one of her relatives, out of dislike for severing ties."
"10501","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Sha'bi, he said: it is not proper for a man to join together two women, such that if one of them had been a man it would not have been lawful for him to marry her. Sufyan said: its explanation with us is that it be through lineage, and it is not like a woman and the daughter of her husband, whom he may join together if he wishes."
"10502","From Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, he said: I asked al-Qasim ibn Muhammad: may a woman be married over her maternal aunt or over her paternal aunt? He said: no, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that. I said to him: he has already entered with her, and he has taken responsibility for her — are they then separated? He said: I do not know. He said: so I asked Mujahid, and he said to him the like of the saying of al-Qasim about all that; then I asked Amr ibn Shu'ayb, and he said: he shall not marry her. So I said: she has already taken responsibility; he said: and that they be separated. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade that a woman be married over her paternal aunt or over her maternal aunt."
"10503","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Hasan ibn Muhammad informed him that Hasan ibn Husayn ibn Ali married in one night the daughter of Muhammad ibn Ali and the daughter of Umar ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, thus joining together two daughters of paternal uncles; and that Muhammad ibn Ali said: he is more lawful to us than both of them. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, the like of it. He said: in the morning their women did not know to which of the two to go."
"10504","From Ibn Abi Najih, from Ata, about a man who divorces a woman, then she marries a man and bears him a girl, while his first wife had a son; he said: there is no harm in his son marrying the daughter of his wife by the man she married after him."
"10505","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, that they both said: there is no harm in it. Ma'mar said: and al-Hasan said it also."
"10506","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he used to dislike a man marrying the daughter of a woman his father had had intercourse with: whatever child she bore before his father had intercourse with her, there is no harm in marrying her; and whatever child she bore after his father had intercourse with her, he shall not marry any of her children."
"10507","From Ma'mar, he said: I said to Ibn Abi Najih: do you know anyone who dislikes that? He said: Mujahid used to dislike it. Ma'mar said: and I know no one who dislikes it except what was mentioned from Tawus and Mujahid."
"10508","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Malik ibn al-Mughirah, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about making a woman lawful for her husband, and he said: that is fornication."
"10509","From al-Thawri and Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi', from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: whenever a muhallil or a muhallalah is brought to me, I will stone them both."
"10510","From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Sharik al-Amiri, he said: I heard Ibn Umar being asked about a man who divorced a daughter of his paternal uncle, then desired her and regretted and wanted a man to marry her to make her lawful for him; so Ibn Umar said: both of them are adulterers, even if they remain so-and-so long — and he mentioned twenty years or about that — when Allah knows that he intends to make her lawful for him."
"10511","From al-Thawri and Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Huwayrith, from Ibn Abbas, he said: a man asked him and said: my paternal uncle divorced his wife thrice? He said: your uncle disobeyed Allah and so He made him regret, and he obeyed Satan and so He made no way out for him. He said: what do you think about a man who makes her lawful for him? He said: whoever tries to deceive Allah, He deceives him."
"10512","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: the deliberate muhallil — is there a punishment upon him? He said: I do not know of it, though I think he should be punished. He said: and all should be inclined against that, the old and those who magnify the dower."
"10513","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: if the marrying man, or the one giving in marriage, or the woman, or any one of them intended tahleel, then it is not valid."
"10514","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, that he used to see no harm in tahleel when neither of the two spouses knew."
"10515","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: if the muhallil divorces her, she does not become lawful for her first husband; they are separated when his marriage was in the manner of tahleel."
"10516","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: a person married a woman as a deliberate muhallil, then desired her and kept her? He said: there is no harm in that."
"10517","From Ma'mar, from one who heard al-Hasan saying, about a man who married a woman to make her lawful, without informing her: al-Hasan said: fear Allah, and do not be a nail of fire in the limits of Allah."
"10518","From Hisham, from Ibn Sirin, he said: a woman sent to a man and married herself to him to make her lawful for her husband; so Umar ordered him to stay with her and not divorce her, and threatened him with consequence if he divorced her. He said: and he was poor, owning nothing; he had two patches, joining one over his front and the other over his back, and he was called Dhu al-Ruq'atayn. From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, the like of it."
"10519","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Mujahid said: a man of Quraysh divorced a woman and made it final, and passed by an old man and a son of his, Bedouins in the market, who had come for trade of theirs; so he said to the youth: is there good in you? Then he passed on from him, then returned to him and spoke to him. He said: yes; so show me your hand. Then he went off with him and told him the matter, and ordered him to marry her; so he spent the night with her. In the morning he sought permission for him and permission was given, and he had become attached to her; so she said: by Allah, if he divorces me I will never marry you. That was mentioned to Umar, so he called him and said: had you married her I would have done so-and-so to you. So he threatened him, then called her husband and said: keep her."
"10520","Ibn Jurayj said, and another than Mujahid said: a man divorced his wife in the time of Umar and made it final; and there was a poor man in Madinah, I think from the Bedouins, called Dhu al-Namiratayn. An old woman came to him and said: do you want a marriage, and a dower, and witnesses, and you spend the night with her, then in the morning you leave her? He said: yes. So that happened, and he spent the night with her; then in the morning she clothed him with a robe and said: I am staying with you, and he asks you to divorce me. So he went to Umar; Umar called the old woman and beat her severely, and said: by Allah, if proof stands for me... and said: praise be to Allah who clothed you, O Dhu al-Namiratayn; keep your wife, and if any man casts doubt upon you, come to me."
"10521","From Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, he said: there is no harm in it when the husband did not order it."
"10522","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the muhill and the one for whom it is done, and the eater of riba, and the witness, and the scribe, and the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, and the woman who tattoos and the one who is tattooed and the one for whom it is tattooed."
"10523","From Jabir, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cursed the eater of riba and its giver, and its two witnesses, and its scribe, and the woman who tattoos and the one tattooed for beautification, and the withholder of charity, and the muhill and the one for whom it is done, and he used to forbid wailing. From Ma'mar, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Hubhab, from al-Sha'bi, from al-Harith, from Ali, the like of it."
"10524","From Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Harith, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: the eater of riba and its giver, and its witness and its scribe when they know of it, and the woman who joins hair and the one for whom it is joined, and the distorting collector of charity and the transgressor in it, and the one who turns back upon his heels as a Bedouin after his migration, and the muhallil and the one for whom it is done, are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the Day of Resurrection."
"10525","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: concerning the slave who finally divorces the slave woman — her master making her lawful for him to have intercourse with her."
"10526","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata: the slave divorces the slave woman and makes it final — is it lawful for her master to have intercourse with her? He said: yes. I said: even if he only intended thereby tahleel? He said: no, tahleel has been forbidden."
"10527","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam and Zayd ibn Thabit, that they used to say: the slave woman becomes lawful for her husband for her master to have intercourse with her, when he does not intend tahleel."
"10528","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a woman whom her husband divorced and then her master had intercourse with her; he said: when he did not intend making lawful, there is no harm in her husband taking her back. And Ma'mar said: and it reached me from Zayd ibn Thabit the like of that."
"10529","From al-Thawri, from Ma'mar, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: she does not become lawful except from where she was made unlawful."
"10530","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, he said: al-Sha'bi was asked: what do you think, if her master fell upon her? He said: he is not a husband."
"10531","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il al-Asadi, from al-Sha'bi, about the master making the slave woman lawful for her husband; he said: none makes her lawful except a husband."
"10532","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: none makes her lawful except a husband."
"10533","He said: from Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed from Amir and Masruq and Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to say: the intercourse of her master does not make her lawful for her husband until she marries a husband other than him."
"10534","From Hushaym, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Marwan al-Asghar, from Abu Rafi', he said: Uthman ibn Affan and Zayd ibn Thabit were asked, with Ali ibn Abi Talib present, about the slave woman — does her master make her lawful for her husband when he does not intend tahleel? They said: yes. He said: Ali disliked their saying and stood up angry."
"10535","From Ma'mar, from al-Ash'ath, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara ibn Azib, from his father, he said: I met my uncle with a banner with him, and I said: where are you heading? He said: the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and ordered me to kill him."
"10536","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: a man marries a woman and does not see her until he divorces her — does she become lawful for his son? He said: no, it is general in the Quran. I said: except what has already passed? He said: in the pre-Islamic age, sons used to marry the wives of their fathers."
"10537","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: she does not become lawful for his son, nor for his father. He said: I said: then what is His saying, except what has already passed? He said: in the pre-Islamic age, a man used to marry his father's wife."
"10538","From Ma'mar and al-Thawri, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: when a man marries a woman and did not consummate with her? He said: she does not become lawful for his father, nor for his son."
"10539","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Umayr, freedman of Ibn Abbas, he said: Ibn Abbas said: seven are forbidden through lineage and seven through marriage ties; then he recited: and your mothers who nursed you, until he reached: and that you join together two sisters; and he recited: and do not marry what your fathers married of women; and he said: this is the marriage tie."
"10540","Ma'mar reported to us, from Qatadah, that Ibn Mas'ud said: Allah forbade twelve women, and I dislike twelve: the slave woman and her sister, and two sisters joined together, and the slave woman when your father had intercourse with her, and the slave woman when your son had intercourse with her, and the slave woman when she is given deferred freedom, and the slave woman in the waiting period of another than you, and the slave woman who has a husband, and your slave woman who is a polytheist, and your paternal aunt and your maternal aunt through fosterage. Abd al-Razzaq said: the Arabs used to forbid all lineages in the pre-Islamic age, and those with inviolable ties, except two sisters joined together, and the father's wife — for they used to join together two sisters and marry the father's wife."
"10541","From al-Thawri, from Abu Farwah, from Abu Amr al-Shaybani, from Ibn Mas'ud, that a man of Banu Shamkh ibn Fazarah married a woman, then saw her mother and she pleased him; so he sought the verdict of Ibn Mas'ud, and he ordered him to separate from her, then marry her mother; so he married her and she bore him children. Then Ibn Mas'ud came to Madinah and asked about that, and was informed that she is not lawful for him. When he returned to Kufah, he said to the man: she is forbidden for you; she is not proper for you, so separate from her."
"10542","From Ma'mar, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, that Ibn Mas'ud gave a concession about it; then he came to Madinah and was informed of what contradicted his saying, so he retracted it and said: I think Umar is the one who turned him back from it."
"10543","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: Imran ibn Husayn was asked about it, and he said: it is of what was forbidden. He said: and Masruq ibn al-Ajda' was asked about it, and he said: it is left unspecified, so leave it."
"10544","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he disliked it."
"10545","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, that he used to dislike it. Ma'mar said: and it reached me from al-Hasan the like of the saying of al-Zuhri."
"10546","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: she is not lawful for him; it is general. I said: did Ibn Abbas recite it: and the mothers of your wives whom you entered? He said: no. He disavowed."
"10547","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me that Mujahid said to him: and the mothers of your wives and your stepdaughters who are in your care — entry was intended for both together."
"10548","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying, about a man who marries a woman and then she dies before he touches her: he may marry her mother if he wishes."
"10549","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs informed me, from Muslim ibn Uwaymir al-Ajda', of Bakr ibn Kinanah, he informed him that his father married him to a woman in Taif. He said: I had not yet joined her when my uncle died leaving her mother, and her mother possessed much wealth; so my father said: do you want her mother? He said: so I asked Ibn Abbas and told him the matter, and he said: marry her mother. He said: so I asked Ibn Umar, and he said: do not marry her. So I told my father what Ibn Abbas said and what Ibn Umar said, and he wrote to Mu'awiyah and informed him in his letter of what Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas said; so Mu'awiyah wrote: I do not make lawful what Allah forbade, nor forbid what Allah made lawful; you and that matter — and women are many. So he neither forbade me nor permitted me; and my father turned away from her mother and did not marry her to me."
"10550","From al-Thawri, about a man who married a woman and her daughter in one contract: he is separated from both, and they get no dower when he had not entered with either of them; and he may marry her daughter afterwards if he wishes. Then if he married the mother and did not enter with her, he may marry the daughter if he wishes; and if he married the daughter and did not enter with her, he may not marry the mother."
"10551","One who heard al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah informed me, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whatever man marries a woman, whether he entered with her or did not enter with her, her mother is not lawful for him."
"10552","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: and your stepdaughters who are in your care — what is entry with them? He said: that she be conducted to him as a bride, and he uncovers and sits between her legs. I said: if he did that with her in the house of her family? He said: it suffices him; that has already forbidden her daughters to him. I said to him: yes, but he did not uncover? He said: the stepdaughter is not forbidden to him if he did that with her mother."
"10553","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, about a man who touches or kisses or embraces; he said: her mother and her daughter become disliked."
"10554","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, he said: entry is intercourse itself."
"10555","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I ordered a man to ask Ata about it where I could not hear: if the mother of the stepdaughter was conducted to him as a bride, and he closed the door upon her, but had not touched her — does that forbid the stepdaughter, when she says: he did not do it? He said: yes."
"10556","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, he said: Ibn Abbas said: entry, and covering, and uncovering, and embracing, and rafath, and touching — this is intercourse; except that Allah is modest and generous, expressing by euphemism as He wishes for what He wishes."
"10557","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, he said: they narrate from the companions of Ibn Mas'ud, saying: when a man marries a woman and kisses her out of desire, her daughter becomes forbidden to him, and her mother becomes forbidden. He said: and they say from Ibn Mas'ud: and the slave woman and her daughter are in that position — when he kisses her, her daughter becomes forbidden to him. I said: then the stepdaughter? He said: no."
"10558","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he used to say: entry, and touching, and contact is intercourse; and rafath in fasting is intercourse; and rafath in hajj is incitement to it. Ibn Jurayj said: and Amr ibn Dinar said: entry is intercourse."
"10559","From al-Thawri, he said: there is no harm in marrying the stepdaughter when he had not entered with the mother."
"10560","From one who heard al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrating, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Amr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: whatever man marries a woman and did not enter with her, then he may marry her daughter if he wishes."
"10561","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: when a man looks at the private part of a woman out of desire, she does not become lawful for his son nor for his father."
"10562","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: when a man kisses a woman out of desire, or touches her, or looks at her private part, she does not become lawful for his father, nor for his son."
"10563","From Ma'mar, from Simak ibn al-Fadl, that Ibn al-Zubayr said: the stepdaughter and the mother are alike; there is no harm in both when he had not entered with the woman."
"10564","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah informed me — Abu Sa'id said: I saw in the book of another than Ibn Ubayd — he said: Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan al-Nasri informed me, he said: I had a wife who bore me children and then died, and I grieved over her; so I met Ali ibn Abi Talib, and he said: what is wrong with you? So I said: the woman has died. So he said: does she have a daughter? I said: yes. He said: was she in your care? I said: no, she is in Taif. He said: then marry her. He said: I said: then where is His saying: and your stepdaughters who are in your care? He said: she was not in your care; that is only when she was in your care."
"10565","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibrahim ibn Maysarah informed me that a man of Sawa'ah called Ubaydullah ibn Ma'bad — he praised him well — informed him that his father or his grandfather married a woman with a child by another than him, then married a young woman; so one of the sons of the first said to him: you have married over our mother, and you have grown old and become independent of her by a young woman, so divorce her. He said: no, by Allah, unless you marry me your daughter. So he divorced her and married him his daughter, though she was not in his care, neither she nor her father, the son of the divorced old woman. He said: so I came to Sufyan ibn Abdullah al-Thaqafi and said: seek a verdict for me from Umar. So he said: you shall surely perform hajj with me; and he brought me in to him at Mina. He said: so I told him the matter, and he said: there is no harm in that; go and ask so-and-so, then come and inform me. He said: and I think he said only Ali. He said: so I asked him, and he said: there is no harm in that. He said: so he joined them together."
"10566","I asked Ma'mar: may a man marry the wife of his stepson? He said: there is no harm in her. I said: then the daughter of his stepson? He said: she is not lawful for him."
"10567","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: and the wives of your sons — a man marries a woman and does not see her until he divorces her; does she become lawful for his father? He said: it is general: and the wives of your sons who are from your loins. He said: we hold and narrate, and Allah knows best, that it was revealed concerning Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he married the wife of Zayd; the polytheists in Makkah spoke about that, so there was revealed: and the wives of your sons who are from your loins; and there was revealed: nor has He made your claimed sons your sons; and there was revealed: Muhammad is not the father of any of your men."
"10568","From Ma'mar, he said: I asked al-Zuhri about a man who kissed his slave woman or touched her — may he have intercourse with her mother? He said: no, nor is she lawful for his father, nor for his son."
"10569","From al-Awza'i, from Makhul, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab stripped a slave girl and looked at her, then one of his sons asked him to give her to him; so he said: she is not lawful for you."
"10570","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, that Umar stripped a slave girl and looked at her, then forbade one of his children to approach her."
"10571","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman, the two sons of Amir ibn Rabi'ah, that Amir ibn Rabi'ah — and he was a Badri — forbade them a slave girl of his to approach her; and they said: we did not know of anything from him to her except that he may have glanced at her a glance he disliked us to glance."
"10572","From Ma'mar, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Masruq enjoined his sons, saying: whoever of you buys this slave girl, let him not approach her, for there was from me to her what none of you should approach her after — he mentioned touching or the like of that."
"10573","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, that he said to his sons about a slave girl of his: I sat from her a sitting, or looked from her a look, that I would not like you to sit my sitting nor look my look."
"10574","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, that Masruq ordered them to sell her, saying: I took from her only what forbids her to my child, of touching and looking."
"10575","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: what forbids the father to the child and the child to the father is kissing the slave girl, or placing the hand upon her private part, or embracing her, or placing his private part upon her private part."
"10576","From Ma'mar, from al-Hasan and Qatadah, they said: nothing forbids her to him except intercourse."
"10577","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: and I dislike the slave woman whom your father had intercourse with, and the slave woman whom your son had intercourse with."
"10578","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: when a man looks at the private part of a woman out of desire, she does not become lawful for his son, nor for his father."
"10579","I asked al-Thawri, saying: a man wanted to marry a woman, and his son said: I have already had her unlawfully? He said: if he wishes, he need not believe him."
"10580","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: when a man kisses a woman out of desire, or touching, or looks at her private part, she does not become lawful for his father, nor for his son."
"10581","Ibn Jurayj reported to us, he said: I said to Ata: or the pardon of him in whose hand is the marriage tie? He said: the guardian. I heard Ibn Abbas saying: the nearer of the two to piety is the one who pardons."
"10582","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, he said: I heard Ikrimah, freedman of Ibn Abbas, saying: Ibn Abbas used to say: Allah is pleased with pardon and commanded it; then if she pardons, that is it, and if her guardian in whose hand is the marriage tie pardons and she is pleased, it is allowed; but if she refuses..."
"10583","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: the one in whose hand is the marriage tie is the guardian. He said: and al-Hasan and Ikrimah said it."
"10584","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: the one in whose hand is the marriage tie is the father; and His saying: except that they pardon — it is the woman."
"10585","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me: except that they pardon — he said: it is the previously married woman; or pardons he in whose hand is the marriage tie — he said: the guardian of the virgin."
"10586","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: The one in whose hand is the marriage tie is the guardian."
"10587","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid informed me that Sa'id ibn Jubayr said: It is the husband. And Mujahid said it."
"10588","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, he said: It is the husband."
"10589","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh, he said: It is the husband."
"10590","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: It is the husband."
"10591","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: One whom I trust informed me that Ibn al-Musayyab said: It is the husband; his pardoning is completing the dower in full, and her pardoning is giving up half of it."
"10592","From Ma'mar, from Salih ibn Kaysan, that Nafi ibn Jubayr married a woman then divorced her before building with her, and he completed the dower for her, interpreting the one in whose hand is the marriage tie to mean the husband. Ma'mar said: Except that they pardon means the women, in the view of all of them, whether he who said it is the husband or he who said it is the guardian; and they say they pardon meaning they forgo the dower."
"10593","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, that Umar and Ali said: When the curtains are let down and the doors are closed, the dower has become obligatory. Al-Hasan said: She has the dower and upon her is the waiting period."
"10594","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: It has reached us that when she is brought to him and he closes the door upon her, the dower becomes obligatory even if he did not touch her, even if she is found a virgin, and even if she is menstruating; that is the Sunnah."
"10595","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When the doors are locked, the dower, the waiting period, and inheritance become due, and he may take her back so long as he has not made her divorce final; and if he says I did not touch her and she also says the same, they are not believed."
"10596","Ibn Jurayj reported from Ibn Shihab about a man who married a woman and consummated with her, then divorced her after two days; the woman was asked and said he did not touch me, and the man was asked and said the same, and he said: When he entered upon her and let down the curtains over her, the dower has become obligatory and upon her is the waiting period. Then he informed me from Sulayman ibn Yasar that al-Harith ibn al-Hakam married a strange woman and entered upon her, and she turned out to be dusky, so he did not uncover her as he had said, and he was ashamed to leave at once, and he said: he stayed with her in privacy, then Marwan came and sent, then he left and divorced her, so she has half the dower, and he said I did not uncover her, and she disputed that with him, so that was raised to Marwan, and Marwan sent to Zayd ibn Thabit and said to him: O Abu Sa'id, a righteous man, his affair was such and such, and he is trustworthy, is there upon him but half the dower? Zayd said to him: What if the woman were now pregnant? He said: It is from him, would you carry out the hadd upon him? Marwan said: No. Zayd said: Rather she has her full dower. So Marwan judged with that."
"10597","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him that Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan regretted his judgment about the daughter of Abu Zuhayr. Amr said: And they say: If she was brought to him and he said I did not touch her, if she admits that, she has the full dower."
"10598","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: When the curtains are let down and the doors are closed, the dower has become obligatory."
"10599","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: Umar ibn al-Khattab judged about the man who marries, when the curtains are let down over him and the doors are closed, the dower has become obligatory."
"10600","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed me, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab say: Umar ibn al-Khattab judged about the man who marries, when the curtains are let down over him, the dower has become obligatory upon him. From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Umar, the same."
"10601","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar said: When the curtain is let down and the door is closed, the dower becomes obligatory."
"10602","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: Umar said: What is their fault if the incapacity comes from your side? She has the full dower and the full waiting period."
"10603","From Ma'mar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Umar ibn al-Khattab judged about a man who was alone with a woman but did not mingle with her, that the dower is complete, saying: When he is alone with her even if he did not close a door nor let down a curtain."
"10604","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman, he said: Awf narrated to us, he said: I heard Zurarah ibn Awfa say: The rightly guided rightly guiding caliphs judged that whoever closes a door and lets down a curtain, the dower has become obligatory upon him."
"10605","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Abd al-Malik judged about the daughter of Abu Zuhayr with half the dower, and he said: People indeed criticized his judgment with that."
"10606","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, from al-Hasan, that Umar and Ali said: When he is alone with her and closes the door upon her or lets down the curtains, the dower has become obligatory. And Sulayman ibn Musa added, from Umar: And the waiting period and inheritance."
"10607","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, that Ibn Mas'ud said the same as the saying of Umar. I said to Abd al-Karim: And if he was alone with her in an open space? He said: It suffices him, it has become obligatory. Abd al-Karim said: If he was alone with her in his house or in her family's house and closed the door upon her or let down a curtain, that suffices him equally. If she was a virgin, that is not looked at in her case, and likewise if she was menstruating. If both of them together say he touched her, it is upon what they said; and if both together say he did not touch her, it is upon what they said, and she has half the dower. And they said: She lies about the waiting period fearing she may want another. If she says he touched her and he denies, she is believed and he is disbelieved, but she swears for him if he wishes. If she says he did not touch her and he says rather I did touch her, then perhaps she has desired another and wants him now, and she does not observe waiting; Shurayh judged about her: She is believed about herself regarding her dower, she has half of it, and she observes the waiting period of a divorced woman for another."
"10608","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah informed me, from his father, he was asked about a man who marries a woman and she stays with him a year and months, he takes from her less than intercourse, then divorces her before touching her. He said: She has the full dower and upon her is the full waiting period."
"10609","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The full dower does not become obligatory until he has intercourse with her, even if he closed the door upon her. I said: And when the dower becomes obligatory, does the waiting period become obligatory? He said: Does anyone say other than that?"
"10610","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: She has half the dower."
"10611","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Layth informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The dower does not become obligatory until he has intercourse with her; she has half of it."
"10612","From al-Thawri, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: She has the half."
"10613","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Minhal ibn Umar, and from Hayyan ibn Marthad, from Ali, he said: When the curtains are let down and the door is closed, the dower has become complete."
"10614","From Ja'far ibn Sulayman, he said: Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed me that he witnessed Shurayh, and a man who entered upon a woman was brought to him, and he said I did not touch her, and she said he spoke the truth, so he judged for her half the dower, and people criticized that against him, so he said: We strike between them with the Book of Allah. And Ma'mar said, from Shurayh: She is believed by her admission against herself regarding the dower, and she has half of it, and the waiting period is obligatory upon her."
"10615","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that he said about a woman whom a man entered upon and she stayed with him a time, and he could not do it with her: He judged for her the half, and upon her is the waiting period."
"10616","From Ibn al-Taymi, Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid informed us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: Amr ibn Nafi came to Shurayh disputing with a woman of his whom he had divorced; she claimed he entered upon her, and he denied he did it, so he ordered him an oath, and he swore by Allah he never entered upon her at all, and he said: Give her half the dower."
"10617","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who married a woman and drove the dower to her before entering upon her, then divorced her before entering upon her, and fire consumed the goods. He said: She is liable; she returns to him half of what he gave her."
"10618","From Ubayd Allah and Abd Allah, the two sons of Umar, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar married his son Waqid, and he died before entering or fixing a dower, and Ibn Umar assigned her no dower, but her mother refused but to dispute, so Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd came to him and said: Her mother has refused but to dispute with you, and the saying is as you say. Ibn Umar said: I do not like that you leave a right if it is yours. So she disputed with him to Zayd ibn Thabit, and Zayd assigned her no dower, and assigned her inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period. From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"10619","From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, similar to that, and he mentioned that Ibn Umar married the daughter of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar."
"10620","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard him say: Inheritance suffices her, and she has no dower, and upon her is the waiting period."
"10621","From al-Thawri, and Ja'far, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abd Khayr, from Ali: that he used to assign her the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period, and he assigned her no dower."
"10622","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that Ali used to assign her the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period, and he assigned her no dower. Al-Hakam said: He was told of the saying of Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: The Bedouins are not believed against the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"10623","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: Inheritance suffices her, she has no dower. And Ibn Uyaynah said, from Amr, and from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: Upon her is the waiting period. Amr said: I heard Ata and Abu al-Sha'tha say that."
"10624","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he used to say: She has no dower, until he heard the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud, then he held back from it and said nothing about it."
"10625","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I heard Ata say: I heard Ibn Abbas being asked about a woman whose husband dies and he had fixed a dower for her. He said: She has her dower, and she has the inheritance."
"10626","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, he said: Abdullah ibn Mas'ud was asked about a man who married and fixed nothing for her and did not touch her until he died. He gave a ruling for them, then said: I speak in it by my opinion; if it is right it is from Allah, and if it is wrong it is from me. I see for her the dower of a woman of her peers, neither too little nor too much, and upon her is the waiting period, and she has the inheritance. So Ma'qil ibn Sinan al-Ashja'i stood and said: I bear witness you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Barwa' bint Washiq, a woman of Banu Ruwas of Banu Amir ibn Ruwas ibn Sa'sa'ah. And Sufyan holds with it."
"10627","From Ma'mar, from Asim, from al-Sha'bi, that a man came to Abdullah ibn Mas'ud and asked about a woman whose husband died, and he had not entered upon her nor fixed for her. Ibn Mas'ud said: Ask the people, for people are many, or as he said. The man said: By Allah, if I knew for a whole year I would find none but you, I would not leave you. He said: So he put him off a month. Then Ibn Mas'ud stood and performed ablution, then prayed two rak'ahs, then said: O Allah, whatever is right is from You, and whatever is wrong is from me. Then he said: I see for her the dower of one of her womenfolk, and inheritance with that, and upon her is the waiting period. So a man of Ashja' stood and said: I bear witness you have judged in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Barwa' bint Washiq al-Aslamiyyah, who was under Hilal ibn Umayyah. Ibn Mas'ud said: Did anyone hear this with you? He said: Yes. So he brought a group of his people and they testified to that. He said: Ibn Mas'ud was never seen rejoicing at anything as he rejoiced at that, when it agreed with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). From Ma'mar, he said: Al-Hasan and Qatadah used to speak in it upon the saying of Ibn Mas'ud."
"10628","From Ma'mar, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me that his father used to say: She has no dower, until he heard the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud. He said: Then he held back from it and said nothing about it."
"10629","From al-Thawri, he said: The dower is all due at once for her when she asks for it, its prompt and its deferred, unless he fixes a time."
"10630","From Hisham, from al-Hasan, he said: The dower is due at once; whenever she wishes she takes it. And Muhammad ibn Sirin said, from Shurayh: Until he divorces."
"10631","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, he said: The woman binds her husband for her dower so long as he has not entered upon her; when he has entered upon her, she has nothing."
"10632","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: A man married in addition to his wife, and she came to Shurayh wanting to take him for her dower, and Shurayh said: Allah has permitted two, three, and four; if he divorces you, we shall take it for you for your dower."
"10633","From al-Thawri, from Isma'il, from al-Sha'bi, about a man who married a woman for a known dower then entered upon her, and he says: I have paid you in full, and she says: No; the saying is hers, and his entering is not what obligates her anything except that he bring proof of payment. From Ma'mar, from Ibn Shubrumah, the same; from al-Thawri, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, the same. Sufyan said: If he does not establish proof, then her oath, and she takes her dower. And when a man marries a woman for a named dower, it is all due at once upon him, and she may refuse until he pays her dower in full."
"10634","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, and Ibn Abi Layla, about a man who marries a woman, and she says: He married me for a thousand, and he says: I married her for five hundred. Hammad said: She has the dower of her peers, between it and what she claimed. Ibn Abi Layla said: The saying is the man's unless she establishes proof, and the marriage in both their views is not rejected."
"10635","Abu Sa'id Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-A'rabi reported to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, he said: We read to [blank] from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: The absolution of the father for a virgin is permitted even if she dislikes, and it is not permitted for a previously married woman."
"10636","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: A man may divorce on behalf of his small son so long as he has not had a wet dream, and he says: It is like marriage."
"10637","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: What the father forgoes of his virgin daughter's dower without divorce is permitted, and it is not permitted for a previously married woman. I said: May a man dispose in the dower of his orphan virgin sister without her command? He said: No. I said: May he bargain down in it? He said: No."
"10638","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The absolution of the father for a virgin is permitted, and it is not permitted for a previously married woman."
"10639","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, and Qatadah, they said: The settlement of the father is permitted for his small son who has not reached puberty, and for his small daughter who has not reached puberty."
"10640","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: A dispute was brought to Shurayh about a man who forwent a thousand of his daughter's dower for her husband. The son of Shurayh said: We have allowed your gift and your kindness, and she is more entitled to the price of her person. Ma'mar said: It has reached me that it is not permitted for a man to reduce his sister's dower except with her knowledge, or seeking her permission. From Hisham, from Muhammad, from Hisham, the same."
"10641","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: What the father settles is not permitted for a previously married woman, nor for a virgin either. He said: The dower stands."
"10642","From al-Thawri, he said: The absolution of the father is not permitted for a virgin nor for a previously married woman; he may not give away her wealth. He said: This is our saying."
"10643","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: The proper form of divorce is that he divorce her pure whenever he divorces her, except that he divorce her days before she menstruates, at the start of her waiting period."
"10644","From Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, he said: The proper form of divorce is at the start of her waiting period, pure before he touches her, then he leaves her until her waiting period elapses; if he wishes to take her back before that, he takes her back."
"10645","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man wants to divorce his wife, let him divorce her when she becomes pure from her menstruation, one divorce without intercourse, then leave her until her waiting period ends. If he does that, he has divorced as Allah commanded him, and he is a suitor among suitors. If he wants to divorce her with three divorces, let him divorce her at each menstruation she becomes pure from, one divorce without intercourse. If she has despaired of menstruation, let him divorce her at each new moon one divorce."
"10646","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The divorce of the waiting period is that he divorce her when she becomes pure from menstruation without intercourse. Ma'mar said: I said to Qatadah: What shall I do? He said: When she becomes pure, divorce her before you touch her. If it occurs to you to divorce her another, leave her until she menstruates the next menstruation, then divorce her when she becomes pure the second time. If you want to divorce her the third, leave her until she menstruates, and when she becomes pure, divorce her the third, then she observes one menstruation, then she marries if she wishes."
"10647","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he used to say: The proper form of divorce is that he divorce her pure without intercourse, and when her pregnancy is evident."
"10648","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He divorces her at the start of her waiting period, pure; and if he likes he leaves her until her waiting period elapses, and if he wishes he divorces her at each purity one divorce."
"10649","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he used not to regard as divorce what opposes the proper form of divorce and the proper course of the waiting period, and that he used to say: He divorces her once then leaves her until her waiting period ends."
"10650","From Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: They used to like that he divorce her once, then leave her until her term elapses. And they used to say: Perhaps Allah will bring about after that a matter; perhaps he will become desirous of her."
"10651","From al-Thawri, from al-A'mash, from Malik ibn al-Harith, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: So divorce them at the start of their waiting period. He said: Pure without intercourse."
"10652","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, he said: Ibn Abbas used to read: So divorce them at the start of their waiting period."
"10653","From al-Thawri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: He said: Whoever wants to divorce according to the Sunnah as Allah commanded, let him divorce her pure without intercourse."
"10654","From Wahb ibn Nafi, that he heard Ikrimah narrate, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Divorce is in four standings: two standings lawful and two standings unlawful. As for the unlawful: that he divorce her when he has intercourse with her, not knowing whether the womb holds anything or not; and that he divorce her while she is menstruating. As for the lawful: that he divorce her for her waiting courses, pure without intercourse; and that he divorce her pregnant with evident pregnancy."
"10655","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Ibn Umar say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them at the start of their waiting period."
"10656","From Ma'mar, he said: I said to al-Zuhri: When he wants to divorce her pregnant three times, how? He said: Upon the count of her courses."
"10657","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from al-Sha'bi, about the divorce of the pregnant woman, he said: He divorces at the new moons."
"10658","From al-Thawri, from al-Ash'ath, from al-Hasan, he said: The pregnant woman is not given more than one divorce until she gives birth; when she has given birth, she has become separated from him. He said: And Hammad said it, from Ma'mar, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, the same."
"10659","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When a woman is divorced pregnant and gives birth, Ibn Abbas said: That is when she has reached her term upon giving birth. He said: And Ibn Abbas recited: And when you divorce women and they reach their term. Ibn Tawus said: And if there was a miscarriage in between, likewise. He said: And if he divorced her not pregnant, then when she becomes pure from the last menstruation, that is when she has reached her term. And Ibn Abbas recited: When they reach their term, retain them in kindness or part with them in kindness. Ibn Abbas said: Then let him take her back then, or release her, and call witnesses. Ibn Jurayj said: I narrated it to Ibn Tawus, from his father, and he affirmed it."
"10660","From al-Thawri, from Amr ibn Muslim, or another, from al-Walid ibn Iqal, he said: I asked Abdullah ibn Shaddad, and Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, and Abu Malik, about a man who divorced his wife thrice while she was pregnant, and they said: She is not lawful for him until she marries a husband other than him."
"10661","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Qilabah, and al-Zuhri said: About a woman whom her husband divorces at each purity one divorce, they said: She observes after the three one menstruation. From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, the same; from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, the same; and al-Zuhri said: They said: She observes after the three one menstruation."
"10662","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: She observes from the first divorce."
"10663","From Ma'mar, or another, from Qatadah, that Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Khilas ibn Amr said: She observes from the last divorce three menstruations."
"10664","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, about a man who divorced his wife once then took her back, and did not have intercourse with her until he divorced her; he used to narrate in it disagreement, most of what he narrated being that she observes from the last divorce when he took her back."
"10665","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: When he takes her back, she observes from the later divorce. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, like the saying of Abu Qilabah."
"10666","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: If he takes her back, she starts the waiting period anew, whether he entered upon her or not."
"10667","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Abu al-Sha'tha say: She observes from the day he divorces her. Ibn Jurayj said: And Amr said it, and Abd al-Karim: From the day he divorced her; and Hasan ibn Muslim, and others, and Tawus."
"10668","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorces a woman and she observes part of her waiting period, then he takes her back in her waiting period, and divorces her without touching her; from which day does she observe? He said: She observes the rest of her waiting period. Then he recited: Then you divorce them before you touch them. Ibn Jurayj said: And I say that is only about marriage, and this is a taking back."
"10669","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Qatadah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, they said: About a man who divorces a woman one divorce and she observes part of her waiting period, then he divorces her another, then she also observes days, then he divorces her; they said: She observes from the first divorce, when he had no intercourse with her in between."
"10670","From Wahb ibn Nafi, that Ikrimah informed him, that he heard Ibn Abbas say: Divorce is in four ways: two ways lawful and two ways unlawful. As for the lawful: that he divorce her pure without intercourse, or pregnant with evident pregnancy. As for the unlawful: that he divorce her menstruating, or when he has intercourse with her, not knowing whether the womb holds a child or not."
"10671","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata used to dislike that a man divorce his wife menstruating, as he disliked that he divorce her in childbed."
"10672","From Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he ordered him to take her back and leave her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure, then if he wishes he keeps after, and if he wishes he divorces. That is the waiting period which Allah ordered that women be divorced for. From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, the same."
"10673","Ma'mar reported to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar had divorced his wife once while she was menstruating, and Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it to him, so he ordered him to take her back, then leave her until when she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure, he divorces her. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That is the waiting period which Allah ordered that women be divorced for, meaning: when she becomes pure."
"10674","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, and Sa'id ibn Jubayr, that Ibn Umar had divorced his wife whom he divorced in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) menstruating, and that was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered him to take her back, then leave her, until when she menstruated, then became pure, he divorces her before he touches her. He said: That is the waiting period which Allah ordered that women be divorced for."
"10675","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Shaqiq Abu Wa'il, that Ibn Umar divorced a woman while she was menstruating, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to take her back, then divorce her when she becomes pure."
"10676","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: We sent to Nafi while he was combing in Dar al-Nadwah going to Madinah, and we were sitting with Ata: Was the divorce of Abdullah divorcing his wife menstruating in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counted as one? He said: Yes."
"10677","From al-Thawri, from Asim, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Ibn Umar was asked: Was it counted for you? Meaning: The divorce with which he divorced her while she was menstruating. He said: What prevents me, if I was incapable and foolish?"
"10678","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, he said: I stayed twenty years hearing that Ibn Umar divorced his wife whom he divorced in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) menstruating thrice, until Yunus ibn Jubayr informed me that he asked him. He said: How many did you divorce your wife in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Once."
"10679","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me that he heard Ibn Umar, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayman, freedman of Urwah, asked him: What do you see about a man who divorced his wife menstruating? He said: Abdullah ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was menstruating in the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Umar asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let him take her back. So he returned her and did not regard it as anything. He said: When she becomes pure, let him divorce or keep. Ibn Umar said: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) read: O you who believe, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period at the start of their waiting period."
"10680","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, that he heard Ibn Umar being asked about a man who divorced his wife menstruating. He said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? He said: Yes. He said: He divorced his wife menstruating, so Umar went to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, and he ordered him to take her back. He said: I did not hear him add to that."
"10681","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: He divorced her menstruating? He said: He returns her until when she becomes pure, he divorces or keeps."
"10682","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: Is a woman in childbed who is not menstruating divorced? He said: Her affair is the affair of one divorced menstruating."
"10683","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, that a man divorced his wife while she was menstruating thrice, and he asked Ibn Umar, and he said: You disobeyed your Lord, and she has become separated from you; she is not lawful for you until she marries a husband other than you."
"10684","From al-Thawri, from Layth, from al-Sha'bi, from Shurayh, that a man divorced his wife thrice while she was menstruating: Does she observe after this menstruation three menstruations, and not count this menstruation in which he divorced her? He said: It is what people hold."
"10685","From Hisham ibn Hassan, from Qays ibn Sa'd, freedman of Nafi, from a man he named, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he said about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating: The divorce binds him, and she observes three menstruations besides that menstruation."
"10686","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: When a woman is divorced menstruating, she does not count that, and she starts the menstruations after it. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, and Qatadah, the same."
"10687","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: He divorces her menstruating? He said: She does not count it, to complete three menstruations. I said: And he divorced her the moment she menstruated? He said: She does not count it. He said: It has reached us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Umar: Return her until when she becomes pure, then divorce or keep."
"10688","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: And if he divorced her in childbed when she gave birth, she observes besides her childbed her courses, whatever they were."
"10689","From al-Thawri, he said: The woman in childbed is like the menstruating woman; she does not count her childbed in her waiting period."
"10690","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Amr ibn Dinar: He divorced a woman in childbed who is not menstruating? He said: Yes."
"10691","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, he said: I said to him: If he divorced her menstruating, the Sunnah is that he take her back, until when she becomes pure he divorces or keeps; then she was one menstruation, and she did not count that menstruation? He said: Yes."
"10692","From Uthman ibn Matar, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, he said: He was asked about a man who divorced his wife thrice while she was menstruating, and he said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and Abu Ma'shar, from Ibrahim, they said: She counts it among her courses. And Matar said, from al-Hasan, he said: It is a course among her courses."
"10693","From al-Thawri, about a man who divorced a virgin menstruating, he said: There is no harm in it, because there is no waiting period for him."
"10694","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: He wrote to her with one divorce, then took her back and called witnesses, but the return did not reach her until she married and was touched. He said: The first has nothing, in what has reached us. Then he said that. I said: And he found her when she married and was not touched. He said: The first is more entitled to her. And Abd al-Karim said like his saying."
"10695","From Ibn Jurayj, from Hasan ibn Muslim, that a man divorced his wife while he was absent, then took her back, and she did not know, and the letter did not reach her until she married. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Go, and if you find her and her husband has not entered upon her, you are more entitled to her. From Ma'mar, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and from Mansur, from Ibrahim, the same."
"10696","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, and Mansur, and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, he said: Abu Kanaf, a man of Abd al-Qays, divorced his wife once or twice, then called witnesses to the return but did not convey to her until the waiting period ended, then she married. He came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he wrote to the commander of the city: If the other has entered upon her, she is his wife; otherwise she is the wife of the first. Ibrahim said: And Ali said: She belongs to the first, whether the other entered upon her or not."
"10697","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, that Abu Kanaf divorced his wife, and went out traveling, and called witnesses to her return before the end of the waiting period, with no knowledge of hers of that until she was married. He came to Umar ibn al-Khattab and he wrote for him: If the other has entered upon her, she is his wife; otherwise she belongs to the first. Abu Kanaf came to Kufah and found him not having entered upon her, so he said to women with her: Stand from her, for I have need of her. They stood, and he built with her at once, and she was his wife."
"10698","From Ma'mar, from Ja'far ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam, that Ali said: She is the wife of the latter, whether the first entered upon her or not."
"10699","From al-Thawri, from Abd al-Wahid, from Shurayh, he said: The first has nothing but the fart of the hyena."
"10700","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Ali said about a man who divorced his wife one divorce or two: The return upon her is lawful for her husband until she washes from the third menstruation, and prayer becomes lawful for her. From Ibn Jurayj, from al-Thawri, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from Ali, the same."
"10701","From Ma'mar, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, that Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The return upon her is lawful for her husband until she washes from the third menstruation, and prayer becomes lawful for her. From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, the same."
"10702","From Ma'mar, from Zayd ibn Rufay', from Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, he said: Uthman ibn Affan sent to my father asking him about it, and my father said: How does a hypocrite give fatwa? Uthman said: We seek refuge for you with Allah from being a hypocrite, and we seek refuge with Allah from calling you a hypocrite, and we seek refuge with Allah that there be from you something in Islam, then you die without clarifying it. He said: I see that he is more entitled to her until she washes from the last of the third menstruation, and prayer becomes lawful for her. He said: I know not but that Uthman took with that."
"10703","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: A woman and her husband came to Umar, and she said: O Commander of the Faithful, my husband divorced me and blood ceased from me for three menstruations, then he came to me and I had laid my water and shut my door and taken off my clothes, and he said: I have taken you back. Umar said to Ibn Mas'ud: What do you see? I see she is his wife so long as prayer has not become lawful for her. Umar said: And I see that. From Ibn Jurayj, from Muhammad ibn Murrah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, similar; and Umar said to Ibn Mas'ud: You are for this one, O Abu Abd al-Rahman."
"10704","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, he said: Umar and Ibn Mas'ud said: Until prayer becomes lawful for her."
"10705","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar said to me: The courses are the menstruations. He said: I said to Ata: Is the waiting period purity or courses? He said: It has reached us that she is not free until she washes."
"10706","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar said to me: The courses are the menstruations, from the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Abd al-Karim said: Menstruations; he is more entitled until she cleanses with water and prayer becomes lawful for her. He said: As for the saying of Ibn Umar: Purity, he only took it from Zayd ibn Thabit."
"10707","From Ma'mar, from one who heard Ikrimah, saying: The courses are the menstruations, not purity. Allah, majestic His mention, said: Divorce them for their waiting period, and He did not say: For their courses."
"10708","From Ma'mar, from Qatadah, and Ayyub, from al-Hasan, he said: A man took back his wife when she had laid her clothes wanting to wash, and said to her: I have taken you back. She said: No. They disputed, and she washed, and they disputed to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he returned her to him."
"10709","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Qaza'ah informed me, from al-Hasan, about a man who disputed his wife to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he returned her to him."
"10710","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Qaza'ah informed me, from al-Hasan, about a man who disputed his wife to Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and he had divorced her once and had not taken her back, until she entered her washing place to become pure from the last of the three menstruations. The man came until he called witnesses to her return in the washing place and made her hear, and Abu Musa al-Ash'ari judged between them that he adjure her by Allah whether he took her back before she washed. She admitted he had taken her back before she cleansed with water, so he returned her to him. And Isma'il informed me, from al-Hasan, that Abu Musa judged with that, and with him was Ibn Mas'ud, so he consulted him and he agreed with him; then he wrote in it to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he said that also."
"10711","From Ibn Jurayj, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, he said: Except that she see purity, then delay her washing until that prayer passes her; if she does, she has become separated then."
"10712","From al-Thawri, he said, about the saying of one who said: He is more entitled to her until she washes from the third menstruation, that when she wants purity but does not wash, they said: He is more entitled to her until the time of that prayer for which she became pure passes."
"10713","From Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: She does not become separated until she washes from the third menstruation, and prayer becomes lawful for her."
"10714","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Muslim informed me, from Tawus, he said: A man may take back his wife so long as she is in blood."
"10715","From Umar ibn Rashid, he said: Makhul informed me, that he came to Madinah. He said: I met Sulayman ibn Yasar, and he narrated to me that Zayd ibn Thabit used to say: When a man divorces his wife once or twice, and she sees the first drop of her third menstruation, he has no return upon her. I rejected that of his saying. He said: The people of Madinah decried me, and said: This one rejects against Zayd ibn Thabit. So I asked the scholars of the people of Madinah one by one, and they confirmed to me that Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and Abu al-Darda used to give him the return upon her until she washes from the third menstruation."
"10716","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, he said: When the divorced woman enters the third menstruation, she has become separated from her husband and become lawful for husbands. He said: And with it al-Zuhri used to hold."
"10717","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, like the saying of Zayd. He said: When she enters the third menstruation, she has become separated. And A'ishah used to say: The course is purity, not menstruation. From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Harith ibn Hisham, like the saying of A'ishah."
"10718","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that a man called al-Ahwas of the people of Sham divorced his wife one divorce and died when she had entered the third menstruation. That was raised to Mu'awiyah, and he did not know what to say, so he wrote in it to Zayd ibn Thabit, and he wrote to him: When she enters the third menstruation, there is no inheritance between them."
"10719","From Ma'mar, from Zayd ibn Rufay', from Ma'bad al-Juhani, he said: When she washes her private part from the third menstruation, she has become separated from him."
"10720","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu al-Zinad, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Mu'awiyah wrote to Zayd asking him about that, about a man called al-Ahwas al-Shami: his wife menstruated the third and he died, and Zayd said: There is no inheritance between them."
"10721","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorces without making it final; where does she observe? He said: In her husband's house in which she was. I said: What if he permits her to observe among her family? He said: No; he has shared with her then in the sin. Then he recited: And let them not go out except that they commit a clear indecency. I said: Is this verse about that? He said: Yes; and Amr. I said: It was not abrogated. He said: No."
"10722","From Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, and Qatadah, about a man who divorces a woman one or two: He said: She does not observe in her house. Abu Urwah said: She goes out if she wishes for kinship, but spends the night only in her house."
"10723","From Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife one divorce or two, and she would not go out except with his permission."
"10724","From al-Thawri, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, that Shurayh divorced his wife, and concealed the divorce from her until her waiting period ended."
"10725","From Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, or another, that Shurayh divorced his wife, and concealed the divorce from her until she completed the waiting period, then informed her. She went out at once, and he said to her: Your waiting period has passed, and I knew you would not affirm the divorce, so for that I did not inform you."
"10726","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was told that the name of the wife of Shurayh from whom he concealed the divorce was Kabshah."
"10727","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar informed me that al-Zubayr divorced the daughter of Uthman, and she stayed as Allah willed, and it was said to him: You left her neither unmarried nor with a husband. He said: Far from it, her waiting period has ended. That was mentioned to Abdullah ibn Umar, and he said: Evil is what he did."
"10728","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorced his wife and did not call witnesses, nor inform her; when her waiting period ended, he informed her. He said: She observes from the day he informed her. If he dies in the waiting period, she inherits him; if she dies, he does not inherit her."
"10729","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Except that they commit a clear indecency: Adultery, in what we see and know. I said: And His saying: Except that they commit a clear indecency, so they go out for stoning and she is stoned? He said: Yes. Likewise Amr sees, and Mujahid used to say like the saying of Ata."
"10730","From al-Thawri, from Salih, from al-Sha'bi, he said: Except that they commit a clear indecency. He said: Adultery. And another said: Indecency is going out, disobedience."
"10731","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed that Ibn Umar said: Her leaving her husband's house before her waiting period ends is the clear manifest indecency."
"10732","From Mamar, from Ata al-Khurasani, about His saying: Except that they commit a clear indecency, he said: That was before the fixed punishments were revealed, and when a woman committed indecency she was expelled. Mamar said, and Qatadah said: Indecency means defiance. In the reading of Ibn Masud: Except that they become indecent."
"10733","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Ibn Abbas, he said: When she is foul-mouthed with her tongue, that is indecency, and he may expel her."
"10734","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Alqamah, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Ibn Abbas, about His saying: Except that they commit an indecency, he said: It is that she is abusive toward his family."
"10735","From Abdullah ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar divorced his wife with one divorce, and he would seek permission from her whenever he wanted to pass by."
"10736","From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar divorced his wife while she was in the house of Hafsah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Abdullah's path was through her room, and he refused to take that path and would go around from the back of the house, out of dislike of entering upon them without permission."
"10737","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Ibn Umar divorced his wife with one divorce, and he would seek permission from her whenever he wanted to pass by."
"10738","From Mamar, from Qatadah, about His saying: Lodge them where you dwell according to your means, he said: If he has only one house, she shall dwell in a corner of it."
"10739","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorces a woman but does not make it final, should he seek permission? He said: No, but he should give warning, and she should be cautious and adorn herself for him. If he has two houses, he shall place her in one of them, and if he has only one house, he shall place a curtain between him and her."
"10740","From al-Thawri, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, he said: He should alert her by clearing his throat, and greet, and not seek permission."
"10741","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When a man divorces a woman once or twice, he should seek permission from her, and if there is only one house, he shall place a curtain between him and her."
"10742","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: What is lawful for a man from his wife whom he divorces but does not make final? He said: Nothing of her is lawful for him unless he takes her back."
"10743","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May he see her with her outer cloak off? He said: Yes, there is no harm in that. I said: What about uncovered? Abdul Karim said: Nor bareheaded. Amr said: He shall not kiss her nor touch her with his hand."
"10744","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: May he converse with her? He said: Yes, and she should adorn herself for him and present herself to him."
"10745","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, they said: She should present herself to her husband."
"10746","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, about the woman whose divorce was not made final, he said: She presents herself to her husband and adorns herself for him, and he shall not see her hair nor anything forbidden."
"10747","From Mamar, he said: It reached me that when a man divorces his wife once or twice, he shall not kiss her, nor see her bareheaded, nor shall she uncover herself to him, but she should present herself to him."
"10748","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man takes back his wife while he is with her in her town, but conceals her return from her until her waiting period expires? He said: If she marries, he and the two witnesses shall be punished for what they concealed from her."
"10749","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah ibn Ubayd ibn Umayr informed me that Ali struck her husband and the two witnesses because they concealed from her either the divorce or the return."
"10750","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: Ali judged concerning a man who divorced his wife and informed her of the divorce, then took her back and called witnesses, and ordered the two witnesses to conceal the return from her until her waiting period passed: The testimony was established against the two witnesses, and he declared them liars."
"10751","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abu al-Shatha informed him, he said: I disputed with a man among the early reciters about a woman whom her husband divorces then takes back but conceals her return until her waiting period ends. He said: I said: He has nothing. He said: So we asked Shurayh, and he said: The first husband has nothing but the breaking wind of a hyena. He said: If he divorces her and she remains a year or more spending from his wealth until her waiting period ends with no divorce reaching her, and the maintenance is from his wealth apart from the waiting period."
"10752","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A man divorces his wife once and does not call witnesses nor inform her. We did not add to this."
"10753","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, about a man who divorces his wife while he is absent, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her. From al-Thawri, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, likewise."
"10754","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her."
"10755","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me that she observes her waiting period from the day she was divorced."
"10756","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, Mujahid, Sulayman ibn Yasar, Ibn Sirin, and Abu Qilabah, they said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her. Ayyub mentioned it from all of them."
"10757","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day he died or divorced her."
"10758","From Mamar, from Ayyub, he said: Tawus said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her."
"10759","From Ibn Jurayj and al-Thawri, that Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed them that he heard Said ibn al-Musayyab say: When proof is established, it is from the day he divorced her or died leaving her."
"10760","From al-Thawri, from Hammad and Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her."
"10761","From Mamar, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, that he asked Ibrahim about her, and he said: She observes her waiting period from the day he divorced her or died leaving her."
"10762","From al-Thawri, from Ashath, from al-Shabi, from Ali, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day the news reaches her."
"10763","From al-Thawri, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day the news reaches her."
"10764","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from al-Hasan, he said: She observes her waiting period from the day the news reaches her, and she has maintenance. Mamar said: Qatadah said it too."
"10765","From al-Thawri, from Ismail and Sulayman al-Shaybani, from al-Shabi, he said: Whatever she ate after his death from his wealth is taken from her, except the amount of her inheritance."
"10766","Al-Thawri said, and Hammad and Mansur said, from Ibrahim, he said: It is hers as long as she confined herself for him. And the saying of al-Shabi is more beloved to Sufyan."
"10767","From Ibn Jurayj, from Amr, and from Abu al-Shatha, he said: Maintenance is from his wealth apart from the waiting period."
"10768","From Mamar, about the woman divorced once or twice, then the news does not reach her until her waiting period expires: does her husband have return over her, and do they inherit, according to one who says her waiting period is from the day the news reaches her? He said: They do not inherit, nor does he have return over her, according to both groups. Both said it: Qatadah, from Ali and Ibn Masud as I think, and al-Hasan said it."
"10769","From al-Thawri and Mamar, about a man absent from his wife, then he said: I divorced you a year ago, and she said: I have menstruated three times. He said: She observes her waiting period from the day he informed her, and they do not inherit, and the divorce has passed."
"10770","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Have you seen His saying: What Allah created in their wombs? He said: The child, she should not conceal it so that he desires her, and I do not know, perhaps menstruation is with it. So I ordered a man and he asked him while I listened: Is it binding upon her to inform him of her pregnancy though he did not ask her, so that he desires her? He said: She should disclose it and inform her family, and it will reach him. He said: And it is more beloved to me, when her waiting period ends, that he should deliver it."
"10771","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Mujahid said: Nor is it lawful for them to conceal what Allah created in their wombs: The divorced woman, it is not lawful for her to say: I am pregnant while she is not pregnant, nor: I am not pregnant while she is pregnant, nor: I am menstruating while she is not menstruating, nor: I am not menstruating while she is menstruating."
"10772","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: The woman used to conceal her pregnancy until she attributed it to another man, so Allah forbade them that. He said: And their husbands have more right to return them in that. Qatadah said: More right to return them in the waiting period."
"10773","From Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, about the virgin when her husband divorces her: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. From al-Thawri, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, likewise."
"10774","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, he said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who divorces his wife thrice before consummating with her. He said: I do not see one who does that except that he has fallen into sin."
"10775","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Abu Wail, from Ibn Masud, about the woman divorced thrice before consummation with her: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. As for al-Thawri, he mentioned it from Asim, from Zirr, from Ibn Masud, he said: When he divorces thrice before consummation with her, he regarded her as one consummated."
"10776","From Ibn Uyaynah, from a shaykh called Sufyan, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik, and he came out to us to his sitting place, and passed by us and did not greet us until he reached his sitting place, then he turned to us with his face and said: Peace be upon you. So we asked him about a man who divorces a virgin thrice before consummating with her, and he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab used to separate them and pain him with beating."
"10777","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: When a man divorces a virgin thrice, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"10778","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: I asked al-Hasan about a man who divorces a virgin thrice, then Umm al-Hasan said: And what is beyond three? He said: You spoke the truth, and what is beyond three? So al-Hasan gave fatwa by that for a time, then he retracted and said: One separates her, and he may propose to her. He said: By it in his life."
"10779","From al-Thawri, from al-Hasan, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man divorces thrice and did not consummate, she is separated from him until she marries another husband. And if he said: You are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the two are nothing, and he may propose to her if he wishes. Sufyan said: And it is what we adopt, from Abdullah ibn Muharrar, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, likewise."
"10780","From al-Thawri, he said: Jabir informed me, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, about a man who divorces his wife thrice before consummating with her, and he said: It was a knot in his hand, he released it all together. If they were successive, it is nothing. When he says: You are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the two are nothing."
"10781","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Muhammad ibn Iyas ibn al-Bukayr, that Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, and Abdullah ibn Umar were asked about the virgin whom her husband divorces thrice, and all of them said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"10782","From Umar ibn Rashid, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, that a man from Muzaynah divorced his wife thrice before consummating with her, and he came to Ibn Abbas asking him, and with him was Abu Hurayrah. So Ibn Abbas said: One of the difficult cases, O Abu Hurayrah. Abu Hurayrah said: One separates her, and three forbid her. Ibn Abbas said: You adorned it, O Abu Hurayrah, or he said: You illuminated it, or a word like it, meaning: He was right."
"10783","From al-Thawri, from Muhammad ibn Amr, and from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas, they said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"10784","From Malik, from Yahya ibn Said, from Bukayr, from Numan ibn Abi Ayyash, he said: A man asked Ata ibn Yasar about a man who divorces a virgin thrice, and he said: The divorce of a virgin is only one. Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As said to him: You are a storyteller. One separates her, and three forbid her until she marries another husband."
"10785","From Hushaym, from Jafar ibn Abi Wahshiyyah, from Said ibn Jubayr, he said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband."
"10786","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: When a woman is divorced thrice and they were not joined together, it is only one. That reached me from Ibn Abbas."
"10787","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ibn Abbas said: When a man divorces his wife thrice and did not join them, they are three. He said: So I informed Tawus of that. He said: So bear witness, Ibn Abbas used to regard them as only one."
"10788","From Mamar, from Ayyub, he said: al-Hakam ibn Utaybah entered upon al-Zuhri at Makkah, and I was with him, and they asked him about the virgin divorced thrice. He said: Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah, and Abdullah ibn Amr were asked about that, and all of them said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. He said: So al-Hakam ibn Utaybah went out, and I was with him, and he came to Tawus while he was in the mosque, and leaned over him, and asked him about the saying of Ibn Abbas about her, and he informed him, and informed him of the saying of al-Zuhri. He said: So I saw Tawus raise his hands in astonishment at that, and he said: By Allah, Ibn Abbas used to make it only one."
"10789","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed me, from Yazid ibn Abi Maryam, from Abu Iyad, that Ibn Abbas said: Three and one are the same for the woman not consummated with."
"10790","Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, Ata, and Abu al-Shatha, they said: When a man divorces a virgin thrice, it is one. Amr said: And even if he joins them, it is one."
"10791","From Mamar, from Ibn Tawus, he said: Ikrimah was asked about a man who divorces his virgin wife thrice before consummating with her, and he said: If he joined them, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, and if he separated them, saying: You are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and the two are nothing. He said: So I mentioned that to my father, and he said: It is the same, it is one in every case."
"10792","From Mamar, from Said, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, he said: About a man who divorces a virgin thrice all together and did not consummate with her. He said: She is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. But if he said: You are divorced, you are divorced, you are divorced, she is separated by the first, and he may propose to her. From Mamar, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Shabi, likewise."
"10793","From Abu Sulayman, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam, that Ali, Ibn Masud, and Zayd ibn Thabit said: When he divorces a virgin thrice, joining them, she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband. But if he separates them, she is separated by the first, and the other two are nothing. From more than one, from Mutarrif, from al-Hakam, likewise. From Ibn Uyaynah, from Misar, from Hammad, like their saying."
"10794","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, about a man who divorces the woman he did not consummate with thrice, then takes her back while she thinks he has return over her, and he has intercourse with her. He said: They are separated, and she has a dowry and a half."
"10795","From Mamar, from Hammad, he said: She has her dowry complete, and she also has half the dowry, and they are separated."
"10796","From al-Thawri, from Abu Sahl, from al-Shabi, he said: She has a complete dowry, and they are separated."
"10797","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, like the saying of al-Shabi, they said: She has the dowry complete because of his entering upon her."
"10798","From al-Thawri, from Ismail, from Abu Razin, he said: A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I hear Allah say: Divorce is twice, so where is the third? He said: Release with kindness."
"10799","From al-Thawri, from one of the jurists, he said: A man in the pre-Islamic age would divorce his wife as he wished, with no waiting period upon her, so she would marry on the spot if she wished. Then a man from Ashja came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, he divorced his wife and I fear she will marry, so the child will belong to another. So Allah revealed: Divorce is twice, and this abrogated every divorce in the Quran."
"10800","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: Divorce had no fixed time in the pre-Islamic age; whenever he wished he took her back in the waiting period, and she was his wife, until Allah instituted divorce as three, saying: Divorce is twice, then retain with kindness or release with kindness, the third."
"10801","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: A woman is divorced while they think menstruation has turned away from her, but that is not clear to them, how is that? He said: As Allah Almighty said: When she despairs of that, she observes three months. I said: What does she wait between that? He said: When she despairs, she observes three months."
"10802","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed me that he heard Ibn al-Musayyab say: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Any man who divorces his wife, and she menstruates once or twice, then stops, she shall sit nine months until her pregnancy becomes clear. If no pregnancy becomes clear in the nine months, she shall observe three months after the nine she sat without menstruation."
"10803","From al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn Umar, he said: When she menstruates once or twice, then her menstruation ceases, she observes nine months, then she is released."
"10804","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When her menstruation ceases due to old age or doubt about that, she observes three months until she doubts. If she was young, she observes the extent of pregnancy. If her pregnancy becomes clear, her term is to deliver her burden, and if it does not become clear, she completes a year."
"10805","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Karim informed me, from the companions of Ibn Masud, from Ibn Masud, that when a woman is divorced while they think menstruation has turned away from her, but that is not clear to her, she waits a year. If she does not menstruate in it, she observes three months after the year. If she menstruates in the three months, she observes by menstruation. And if she menstruates but her menstruation is not completed after she observed those three months after the year, do not hasten upon her until it is known whether her menstruation completes or not."
"10806","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man divorces his wife once or twice, and she menstruates once or twice, then despairs of menstruation, she shall begin a waiting period of three months. If she menstruates afterward, she shall observe by what she menstruated, and the months waiting period is demolished, and they inherit while she is in her waiting period, if he owns return. He said: And when a woman is divorced having despaired of menstruation, she shall observe three months. If she observes a month or two months or more of that, then menstruates, she shall begin the menstruation waiting period. If it ceases after that and she despairs of menstruation, she shall begin the months waiting period, and shall not count anything past of her waiting period of months and menstruation."
"10807","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that a man from the Ansar called Habban ibn Munqidh divorced his wife while she was nursing, and on the day he divorced her he was healthy. She remained seven months without menstruating, nursing preventing her menstruation. Then Habban fell ill after he divorced her by months, and it was said to him: Your wife will inherit you if you die. So he said to them: Carry me to Uthman. They carried him, and he mentioned the matter of his wife, and with him were Ali ibn Abi Talib and Zayd ibn Thabit. Uthman said to them: What do you see? They said: We see that she inherits him if he dies, and he inherits her if she dies, for she is not of the old women who despaired of menstruation, nor of the virgins who did not menstruate. She is with him upon her menstruation waiting period, little or much. So he returned to his family and took his daughter from his wife. When she lost nursing, she menstruated once, then another at the new moon. Then Habban died before she menstruated the third. So she observed the waiting period of one whose husband died, and inherited him. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr informed me, then he mentioned like the hadith of al-Zuhri. Ibn Jurayj said: And it reached me from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz likewise about Habban."
"10808","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Yahya ibn Said and Ayyub ibn Musa, from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban, he said: My grandfather had two wives: a Hashimite and an Ansarite. He divorced the Ansarite, then died at the head of the year, and she was nursing. When he died, she said: I have inheritance, and I did not menstruate. That was raised to Uthman, and he said: This is a matter I have knowledge of. Raise it to Ali ibn Abi Talib. Ali saw that she be made to swear at the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: If she swears she did not menstruate three times, she inherits. So she swore. Uthman said to the Hashimite, as if excusing to her: This is the judgment of your cousin, meaning Ali."
"10809","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: It reached me that Habban divorced a wife of his from Banu al-Khazraj while she was nursing, and with Habban at that time was the daughter of Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah ibn al-Harith. He lived until she became lawful as he saw, then Habban died. The Khazraj sister said: I have inheritance in his wealth. That reached Uthman, and he said: I do not know what this is. He advised that she be made to swear at the pulpit upon what she said, as if she said: I did not menstruate after his death except at the head of the year. So she was made to swear, then she inherited."
"10810","From al-Thawri and Mamar, from Mansur and Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that he divorced his wife once or twice, then her menstruation ceased sixteen or seventeen months, then she died. Ibn Masud came and said: Allah confined her inheritance to you, so he inherited from her. From Mamar, from Qatadah and more than one, likewise."
"10811","From Abu Hanifah, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, he said: When a man divorces his wife once or twice, then her menstruation ceases while she was in the waiting period, if he made her divorce final, there is no inheritance between them."
"10812","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, about a man who divorces a virgin who did not menstruate. He said: She observes three months. If menstruation reaches her before three months pass, she takes menstruation. If the third passes, her waiting period has ended, and she shall not take menstruation if she menstruates after. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, likewise."
"10813","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, about a virgin woman divorced who had not menstruated, so she observed a month or two months, then menstruated. He said: She observes three menstruations. From Mamar, from Qatadah, likewise."
"10814","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, about the virgin who did not menstruate and the one who sat from menstruation: her divorce is one each new moon. From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, likewise."
"10815","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: If she observes one menstruation, then sits, she observes three months and does not count the menstruation. Ibn Jurayj said: And I say: If she doubts after menstruation, by the saying of Umar and Ibn Masud."
"10816","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: She observes her courses, whether they are near or far."
"10817","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When she menstruates, her waiting period is upon her menstruation, near or far."
"10818","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abdul Karim and others among the scholars, he said: She observes her courses, whatever they are."
"10819","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata said: She observes her courses, whether they are near or far."
"10820","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu al-Shatha, he said: Her waiting period is menstruation, even if she menstruates only once in a year."
"10821","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, about a woman who menstruates irregularly, menstruating once in three months, once in four months, and once in two months: Her waiting period is upon her menstruation if she menstruates."
"10822","From al-Thawri, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, about a woman who menstruates irregularly, he said: When she menstruates, her waiting period is menstruation, even if she menstruates only once in a year."
"10823","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Tawus, he said: When a woman menstruates irregularly, it suffices her to observe three months. He said: And they say it is because of nursing women who hardly menstruate."
"10824","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, he said: She observes three months."
"10825","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from Ikrimah, he said: When she menstruates irregularly, it is doubt, and her waiting period is three months."
"10826","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: When she menstruates once in months, her waiting period is a year."
"10827","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: When she menstruates, her waiting period is upon her menstruation, whether near or far."
"10828","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me, from Abu al-Shatha, that he used to say about her: She observes her courses, whatever they are."
"10829","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, he said: The woman with prolonged bleeding observes upon her courses. Mamar said: al-Hasan said it too."
"10830","From al-Thawri, he said: The woman with prolonged bleeding observes the days of her courses that she used to menstruate."
"10831","From Mamar, from Qatadah, he said: The woman with prolonged bleeding observes three months."
"10832","From Mamar, from a man, from Ikrimah, asked about a woman who menstruates and her blood becomes so much that she does not know how her menstruation is? He said: She observes three months, and he says: It is the doubt that Allah mentioned: If you doubt. Ibn Abbas and Zayd ibn Thabit judged by that."
"10833","From Mamar and Ibn Jurayj, that Ibn Shihab informed him, from Urwah, from Aishah, that she informed him that Rifaah al-Qurazi divorced a wife of his and made her divorce final. Then Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr married her after him. She came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, she was with Rifaah and he divorced her. Ibn Jurayj said: Three divorces, and Mamar said: The last of three divorces. Then she married Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Zubayr after him, and by Allah he has with him, O Messenger of Allah, only like this fringe. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, smiled, then said to her: Perhaps you want to return to Rifaah? No, until you taste his honey and he tastes your honey. She said: And Abu Bakr was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and Khalid ibn Said ibn al-As was sitting at the door of the room, not admitted. Khalid began calling Abu Bakr and saying: O Abu Bakr, will you not rebuke this woman for what she speaks aloud before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"10834","From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, he said: The daughter of Hafs ibn al-Mughirah was with Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah, and he divorced her once. Then Umar married her after him. It was narrated that she is barren and does not bear children, so Umar divorced her before consummating with her. She remained through the life of Umar and part of the caliphate of Uthman. Then Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah married her while he was ill, so that she would share his wives in inheritance, and there was kinship between him and her."
"10835","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed me, from Ibn Abbas, like the hadith of Umar, or Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, and he added: She sat, then came to him after and informed him that he had touched her. So he prevented her from returning to her first husband, then said: O Allah, if it is only by her to make her lawful for Rifaah, his marriage to her shall not be completed another time. Then she came to Abu Bakr and Umar in their caliphates, and they prevented him."
"10836","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata al-Khurasani informed me, from Ibn Abbas, that the woman whom Rifaah al-Qurazi divorced, her name is Tamimah bint Wahb ibn Abd, and she is from Banu al-Nadir."
"10837","From al-Thawri, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Razin, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked while on the pulpit about a man who divorces his wife, then another man marries her, lowers the curtain, uncovers the veil, and closes the door: Is she lawful for the first? He said: No, until she tastes the honey."
"10838","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: No, until she tastes the honey of the one who married her."
"10839","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, he said: I saw Ali, and he was asked about her, so he brought out a hairy forearm of his and said: No, until he shakes her with it."
"10840","From Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar said: If a man divorces his wife thrice, then another man marries her after him, then divorces her before consummating with her, then her first husband marries her, doing that while Umar is alive, he would stone her."
"10841","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Mulaykah informed me that al-Harith ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah informed him that Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah only divorced the daughter of Hafs once, then left her until her waiting period ended, then Umar married her, then Umar divorced her, so Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah married her."
"10842","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me that Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah divorced the daughter of Hafs ibn al-Mughirah once or twice, so Umar married her, and he laid aside his cloak, and it was said to him: He has no child by her, so he laid aside her veil at all, then divorced her, so Ibn Abi Rabiah returned and married her."
"10843","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, that he heard him say: Ibn Abi Rabiah divorced the daughter of Hafs once."
"10844","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: Have you seen if her husband makes her final, then a slave of his marries her and has intercourse with her, does that make her lawful for her first husband? He said: Yes. I said: Is the marriage of a slave to a free woman chastity for her? He said: No. I said: Why? He said: Stoning is not like other. Allah Almighty said: She is not lawful for him after until she marries another husband. So it is marriage, and the marriage of a slave is not chastity."
"10845","From al-Thawri, from Jabir, from al-Shabi, about a slave marrying a divorced woman, he said: She returns to her first husband when the slave divorces her."
"10846","From Mamar, he said: When the slave divorces her, she returns to her husband. This is what there is no doubt about."
"10847","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: The woman whom her husband makes final, then an immature boy marries her who has not reached puberty or ejaculation, does that make her lawful for her first husband? He said: Yes, as we see. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: And it reached me from Jabir, from al-Shabi, like the saying of Ata."
"10848","From Hushaym, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, he said: He does not make her lawful, he is not a husband. And the saying of Ata is more beloved to them."
"10849","From Mamar: And he was asked about her, he said: I did not hear anything about this, but al-Zuhri says: If a woman commits adultery with a boy who has not reached puberty, and he is near it and capable of that, she is stoned."
"10850","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn al-Musayyab and Ubaydullah and others, that they heard Abu Hurayrah say: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Any woman whom her husband divorces once or twice, then leaves her until she marries another husband, and he dies leaving her or divorces her, then her first husband marries her, she is with him upon what remains of her divorce."
"10851","From Malik and Ibn Uyaynah, from al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Ibn al-Musayyab, Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, Ubayd ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, and Sulayman ibn Yasar, all of them say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I heard Umar say: Any woman whom her husband divorces once or twice, then leaves her until she marries another husband, and he dies leaving her or divorces her, then her first husband marries her, she is with him upon what remains of her divorce. From Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn Said, from Ibn al-Musayyab, from Umar, likewise."
"10852","From Mamar, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: I asked Umar about something I was asked about in Bahrain, and Abu Hurayrah was with al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, about a man who divorces his wife once or twice, then she marries another, then her other husband leaves her, then the first returns to her. He said: She is upon what remains of the divorce."
"10853","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Yahya ibn Said informed me, from Ibn al-Musayyab, that Abu Hurayrah was in Bahrain with al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami, and a man from Abd al-Qays asked him who divorced his wife once or twice, and left her until her waiting period, and another man married her, and divorced her or died leaving her. Abu Said said: I found it in the book of another, and it dropped from my book, then her first husband married her and divorced her twice, so he sought fatwa from Abu Hurayrah, and he gave fatwa that she became lawful from him, and was forbidden to him. Then he came to Umar and informed him the news, and Umar said: By what did you give him fatwa? He informed him, and he said: You were right. And Ali and Ubayy ibn Kab said the saying of Umar too."
"10854","From al-Thawri, from Ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Mazidah ibn Jabir, from his father, from Ali, he said: She is upon what remains of the divorce."
"10855","From Abu Shaybah, that al-Hakam informed him, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Kab, he said: She is upon what remains of the divorce."
"10856","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Imran ibn al-Husayn said: She is upon what remains of the divorce, a new marriage and a new divorce. Qatadah said: Shurayh said: New marriage and new divorce."
"10857","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abu Qazaah informed me, from Imran ibn al-Husayn and Shurayh. Imran said: She is upon what remains of the divorce, and Shurayh said: New marriage and new divorce. So Ziyad judged for Imran, and he was governor in Basra at that time."
"10858","From al-Thawri, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ibn Sirin, he said: Imran said: She is upon what remains of the divorce. And Mamar said it, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Shurayh."
"10859","From Ibn al-Mubarak, from Uthman ibn Miqsam, that he informed him that he heard Nubayh ibn Wahb narrate, from a man among the companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He judged about her that she is upon what remains of the divorce."
"10860","From Mamar, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, he said: She is upon what remains of the divorce."
"10861","From Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, he said: The marriage of the one who married her erased the divorce, so the marriage is new and the divorce is new."
"10862","From Mamar, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, he said: New marriage and new divorce. From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Karim said: Ibn Masud and Shurayh said like the saying of Ata."
"10863","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar: The marriage is new and the divorce is new."
"10864","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hasan ibn Muslim informed me, from Said ibn Jubayr, that he was asked about her, and he said: I asked Ibn Umar about that, and he said: Three are erased, and two are not erased."
"10865","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar and Ibn Tawus informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that he said about her: The marriage is new and the divorce is new."
"10866","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas, they said: Marriage does not demolish divorce. And Shurayh said it, from al-Thawri, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Ibrahim, likewise."
"10867","From Ibn al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Mijlaz, from Ibn Abbas and Shurayh, they said: New marriage and new divorce."
"10868","From al-Thawri and Mamar, they said: For both groups, if the other did not touch her, she is upon what remains of the divorce. Mamar said: al-Nakhai said it, and I did not hear disagreement in it."
"10869","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: The decisive? He said: He is put on oath, so if he intended three, it is three, and if he intended one, it is one."
"10870","From Mamar, from Abdul Karim, from Said ibn Jubayr, about the decisive: It is one and what he intended."
"10871","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah informed him that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him that al-Tawamah bint Umayyah was divorced decisively, so Umar ibn al-Khattab made it one."
"10872","From Mamar, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab was asked about a man who divorces his wife decisively, and he said: One makes final, take her back."
"10873","Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar informed me that Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Jafar informed him that al-Muttalib ibn Hantab came to Umar and said: I said to my wife: You are divorced decisively. Umar said: And what carried you to that? He said: Fate. He said: So Umar recited: O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period, and recited: And if they had done what they are admonished with, it would have been better for them, this verse. Then he said: One makes final, return your wife, it is one."
"10874","From al-Thawri, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Umar, about the empty, the innocent, the decisive, and the separated: It is one, and he has more right to her. He said: And Ali said: It is three, and Shurayh said: His intention, if he intended three it is three, and if he intended one it is one. Sufyan said: And he is made to swear along with being put on oath."
"10875","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Tawus informed me, from his father, about being put on oath: that there was no oath with being put on oath."
"10876","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, he said: Concerning al-battah, it is three."
"10877","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah ibn Utbah: Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn Uthman ibn Affan divorced his wife with al-battah during the rule of Uthman, so separation was made between them, and al-Zuhri used to count it as three."
"10878","From Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, he said: When a man divorces his wife with al-battah, she is separated from him as with three."
"10879","From Ibn Uyaynah, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from al-Shabi, he said: The nephew of al-Harith ibn Rabiah came to Urwah ibn al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, who was governor over Kufah, and Urwah said: Perhaps you came to us visiting with your wife. He said: Where is my wife? He said: I left her with Bayda, meaning his wife. He said: Then she is divorced with al-battah. He said: And she is with her. So he asked, and Abd Allah ibn Shaddad ibn al-Had testified that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, counted it as one, and he is more entitled to her. Then he asked again, and a man from Tayyi called Riyash ibn Adi testified that Ali counted it as three. So Urwah said: This is indeed disagreement. So he sent to Shurayh and asked him, though he had been removed from judgeship, and Shurayh said: Divorce is Sunnah, and al-battah is an innovation, so we stop at his innovation and see what he intended by it."
"10880","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me that Shurayh was summoned by one of their rulers and asked about a man who said to his wife: You are divorced with al-battah. He sought to be excused, but he refused to excuse him, and said: As for divorce, it is Sunnah, and as for al-battah, it is an innovation. As for the Sunnah in divorce, carry it out, and as for the innovation, al-battah, impose it on him according to his intention in it."
"10881","From Ibn Jurayj, from Abd al-Karim, from Shurayh, concerning al-battah, al-bariyyah, al-bainah, al-khaliyyah, and khalawtu minni: he is bound by his oath regarding them."
"10882","From Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Concerning al-khaliyyah and al-bariyyah, he used to count each as three."
"10883","From Mamar, from Ayyub, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, he said: If divorce were a thousand, then he said: You are divorced with al-battah, all of them would go. He has shot the farthest mark."
"10884","From Mamar, from Qatadah, that Ali said: Concerning al-battah, al-bariyyah, and al-bainah, they are three divorces. And it is the saying of Qatadah. From Mamar, from al-Zuhri, that he used to count it as three. Mamar said: al-Hasan also said it."
"10885","From Mamar, from al-Zuhri and Qatadah, concerning khaliyyah and khalawt: They said: It is one, and her husband has more right. Mamar said: al-Hasan also said it."
"10886","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Our companions used to say: Al-battah, al-khaliyyah, al-bariyyah, and al-haram depend on his intention. If he intended three, it is three, and if he intended one, it is one, and he has more right to her, and if he wishes he may propose to her."
"10887","From Ibn Jurayj, he said: I said to Ata: The saying of a man: You are khaliyyah, and khalawti minni. He said: They are the same. I said: You are bariyyah, and binti minni. He said: They are the same. I said: You are bainah, or qad binti minni. He said: They are the same. As for his saying: You are khaliyyah, and you are sarah, or count it, or you are divorced, that is Sunnah and he is not bound by oath in that, and it is divorce. As for his saying: You are bariyyah, or you are bainah, that is what they innovated, so both are bound by oath. If he intended divorce, it is divorce, otherwise not. I said: What if he said: You are divorced, or you are khaliyyah, or you are bariyyah, or you are bainah, or you are sarah, then said: I intended three, and regretted, and loved his wife? He said: He is not bound by oath. I said: And divorce did not come out of his mouth? He said: It suffices him that he made clear; she has separated from him, and it is divorce. And Amr ibn Dinar said: It is only one for what came out of his mouth: you are bariyyah, or khaliyyah, or bainah, or binti minni, or bari'tu minni. He said: And he is bound by oath. I said: If by his saying qad binti minni or bari'tu minni he intended three? He said: It is one."
"10888","From Ibn Saman, he said: al-Miswar ibn Rifah al-Qurazi informed me, from Khansa Muzaynah, that her husband became angry and said: If you come down from this bed, you are khaliyyah. So she jumped from the bed and came down. Her husband came to Marwan, who was governor of Madinah, and sought his verdict. Marwan said: Do you want to make it fall on me? No, by the Lord of the worlds. What did you intend, one or al-battah? The Muzani said: I do not know except that it occurred in my mind that I intended al-battah. Marwan said: It is al-battah, and he separated between them."
"10889","From Ibn Saman, he said: al-Miswar ibn Rifah also informed me, from Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, that he said to his wife: If I ever struck you except one strike with a mijdah, you are khaliyyah. Then he struck her another time with a miswak. He sought the verdict of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, who was governor over Madinah. Umar said to him: What occurred in your mind? He said: It occurred in my mind that I intended al-battah. Umar said: She has separated from you."
"10890","From al-Thawri, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, he said: Whoever divorces or means, it is as he meant among what resembles divorce."
